hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16201","82 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hadrami al-Misri: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiyah ibn Ayyub told us, my grandfather Afiyah ibn Ayyub told me, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr told me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted a piece of a gold chain left from the fay with his staff, saying: How will you be on the day this is hoarded for you? No one answered him. A man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, we wish it were hoarded for us; then whoever is patient would be patient, and whoever is tempted would be tempted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you will be worst tempted."
"16202","83 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, he said: Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan ibn Amr told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out one day, I with him, until we entered the synagogue of the Jews on their festival day. They disliked his entering upon them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Jews, show me twelve men of you who testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Allah will lift from every Jew under the canopy of the sky the anger upon him. They fell silent; no one answered him. Then he repeated to them and no one answered him. Then he said a third time and no one answered him. He said: You refuse; by Allah, I am al-Hashir, I am al-Aqib, and I am al-Muqaffi; whether you believe or disbelieve. Then he left, I with him, until we were about to go out, a man called from behind him: Stay as you are, O Muhammad. He turned, and that man said: What kind of man do you know among you, O company of Jews? They said: By Allah, we know no man among us more knowledgeable of the book of Allah nor more understanding than you, nor than your father before you, nor than your grandfather before your father. He said: I testify by Allah of him that he is the Prophet of Allah whom you find in the Torah. They said: You lie. Then they turned on him and spoke evil of him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You lie; we will not accept your word. He said: We left, we three: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I, and Ibn Salam. And Allah Almighty revealed: {Say: Have you considered, if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, while a witness of the Children of Israel testifies to its like and believes while you are arrogant; indeed Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people}."
"16203","84 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah told us: Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan told us. And narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti: my father told us, Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the spoils on the slain, and that a reinforcement man was companion to him in the campaign of Mutah at the edge of Syria. They met the enemy, and a Byzantine among them on a blond horse, with a gilded saddle, a belt stained with gold, and a sword ornamented with gold, charged the Muslims and pressed them with it. That reinforcement man was subtle toward him until he passed by him and hamstrung his horse; it fell, then he overcame him with the sword and killed him. When Allah routed the Byzantines, proof stood for the reinforcement man that he killed him, so Khalid gave him his sword and a fifth of his wealth. Awf said: I spoke to Khalid ibn al-Walid and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the spoils on the slain for the killer? He said: Yes, but I deemed it much. Awf said: There were words between me and him, and I said: By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of your news. Awf said: When we gathered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Awf mentioned what happened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevented you from giving it to him? Khalid said: I deemed it much. He said: Give it to him. Awf said: I said: What do you think, O Khalid, did I not fulfill for you what I promised you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said to Khalid: Do not give it to him. And he said: Will you not leave my commanders for me."
"16204","85 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Walid ibn Muslim said in his hadith: I met Thawr ibn Yazid and narrated this hadith to him, and he said: Bahir ibn Sad told me of it, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of Safwan."
"16205","86 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi: my father told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned the spoils on the slain to the fighter and did not take a fifth from it."
"16206","87 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti: Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan ibn Amr told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you leave my commanders for me? My likeness and theirs is like a man who bought camels and cattle and pastured them, then brought them to a pond and let them into it; they drank its clear water and left its turbid; its clear is for you and its turbid upon them."
"16207","88 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: We used to perform ruqyah in the pre-Islamic period. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of that? He said: Present your ruqyah to me; there is no harm in ruqyah so long as it is not shirk."
"16208","89 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me. And narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: A man of Himyar killed a man of the enemy and wanted his spoils, but Khalid ibn al-Walid, who was governor over them, prevented him. Awf came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: O Khalid, what prevented you from giving him his spoils? He said: I deemed it much, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give it to him. Khalid passed by Awf and pulled his cloak and said: Did I not fulfill for you what I mentioned to you of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He became angered and said: Do not give it to him, O Khalid. Will you not leave my commanders? Your likeness and theirs is like a man who bought camels and pastured them, then awaited watering them and brought them to a pond; they entered it and drank its clear and left its turbid; its clear is for you and its turbid upon them."
"16209","90 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih: Nuaym ibn Hammad told us, Isa ibn Yunus told us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My nation will split into seventy-odd sects; the greatest in trial against my nation are a people who measure matters by their opinion, declaring the unlawful lawful and the lawful unlawful."
"16210","91 - Narrated Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi: Yusuf ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Marwarrudhi told us, Abu Taqi Abd al-Hamid ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi told us, Madan ibn Sulaym al-Hadrami told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Najih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be, O Awf, when this nation splits into seventy-three sects, one in Paradise and the rest in the Fire? I said: When will that be, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When police abound, slave-girls own, the young ride upon the pulpits, they take the Quran as flutes, mosques are ornamented, pulpits raised, fay taken as circulating wealth, zakat as a fine, trust as spoils, religion studied for other than Allah, a man obeys his wife and disobeys his mother, distances his father, the last of this nation curses its first, the corrupt lead the tribe, the vilest of the people is chief of the folk, and a man is honored out of fear of his evil. On that day that will be, and people will flee on that day to Syria, which will protect them from their enemy. I said: Will Syria be conquered? He said: Yes, soon. Then tribulations fall after its conquest. Then comes a dusty dark tribulation. Then tribulations follow one another until a man of my household emerges called al-Mahdi; if you reach him, follow him and be among the guided."
"16211","92 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla: Hisham ibn Ammar told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, Thawr ibn Yazid told us, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the spoils on the slain for the killer."
"16212","93 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us. And narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi: Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi told us, Baqiyyah told us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among his Companions and said: Do you fear poverty or need, or does this world concern you? For Allah will open for you Persia and Rome, and this world will be poured upon you pouring, until nothing will turn you away afterwards, if you turn, except it."
"16213","94 - Narrated Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Zabriq al-Himsi: my father told us. And narrated Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zabriq al-Himsi told us, Amr ibn al-Harith told us, Abdullah ibn Salim told us, from al-Zubaydi, Yahya ibn Jabir told us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr told him that his father told them, that Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai went out to the people and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to seek refuge from three: from greed where there is no greed, from greed returning to nature, and from greed toward what is not an object of hope."
"16214","95 - Narrated Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Misri al-Makki told us, Abdullah ibn Amr al-Waqii told us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"16215","Shurayh ibn Ubayd from Awf ibn Malik 96 - Narrated Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, my father told us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, that he told them, from Awf ibn Malik, that he had with him a man who taught him the Quran. He said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My companion whom you saw with me bought a bow and gifted it to me; shall I take it from him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No. Then he waited until the turn of the year, then returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), shall I take it? He said: No. Then he waited until the turn of the year and said: Shall I take that bow, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No. He said: Shall I not take it, O Messenger of Allah, while it is with him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you wish, O Awf, to meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with a coal of Hellfire between your shoulders?"
"16216","Sayf from Awf ibn Malik 97 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi told us. And narrated al-Husayn ibn al-Samida al-Antaki: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri told us, both said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Sayf, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged between two men, and the one judged against said: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring him back, or he said: Bring the man to me. He said: Allah loves prudence and blames incapacity; when something overcomes you - or he said the matter - say: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer."
"16217","Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab from Awf ibn Malik 98 - Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi told us, Abdullah ibn Amr told us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the campaign of Tabuk at the end of the pre-dawn, while he was in his tent. I greeted him and said: May I enter? He said: Enter. I said: All of me? He said: All of you. Then he said: Six before the Hour: the first of them the death of your Prophet. Say: One. I said: One. And the second: the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. Say: Two. I said: Two. He said: And the third: a pestilence seizing you like the throat-disease of sheep. Say: Three. I said: Three. He said: And the fourth: wealth flowing among you until a man is given a hundred dinars yet remains dissatisfied with it. Say: Four. And the fifth: a tribulation among you leaving no house of mud-brick nor hair but entering it. Say: Five. I said: Five. And the sixth: a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar; they will gather against you like the bearing of a woman, then betray you and advance with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"16218","Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami from Awf ibn Malik. 99 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi: Abu Asim told us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque with a staff in his hand and saw hanging clusters; he prodded a cluster among them, and in it was dry low-quality dates. He said: Who owns this? If only he had given charity of better than it. The owner of this will eat dry dates on the Day of Resurrection. Then he said: O people of Madinah, you will leave it to the prowlers for forty years. It was said: What are the prowlers? He said: Birds and beasts."
"16219","100 - Narrated Abu Muslim: Abu Asim told us, from Abd al-Hamid, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, that Awf ibn Malik and Ibn Abd Kulal entered the mosque of Hims and saw a gathering. Awf said: What is this? They said: Kab is storytelling. He said: Woe to him, has he not heard the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None should tell stories to people except a commander, one commanded, or an arrogant pretender."
"16220","101 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih: my father informed us, Ibn Lahiah told us, al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami told me, Ziyad ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami told us, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever stands in a station of showing off, Allah will show him off; and whoever stands in a station of seeking repute, Allah will make him reputed."
"16221","Shaddad Abu Ammar from Awf ibn Malik 102 - Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar: Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris told us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm told us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim has three daughters and spends on them until they separate or die except they will be for him a veil from the Fire. A woman said: Or two? He said: And two."
"16222","103 - Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar: Uthman ibn Umar told us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm told us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and a woman dark-cheeked are like these two: a woman widowed by herself who restrains herself upon her daughters until they separate or die."
"16223","104 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, Waki told us, from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, who said: Awf ibn Malik said: O plague, take me to you. They said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The longer the life of the Muslim, the better for him? He said: Yes."
"16224","105 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl told us, from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I fear for you six: rule of fools, shedding of blood, sale of judgment, severing kinship, a generation who take the Quran as flutes, and multitude of police."
"16225","Madi Karib ibn Abd Kulal from Awf 106 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi told us, Jabir ibn Ghanim told us, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Madi Karib ibn Abd Kulal, from Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My Lord Almighty gave me choice between two traits: that half my nation enter Paradise, and intercession."
"16226","107 - Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, both said: Zakariya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh told us, Faraj ibn Fudalah told us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Ibn Abd Kulal, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and camped until, when night came, my eyes stayed awake and sleep did not come to me. I rose and there was no animal in the camp but placing its cheek to the earth, and the highest thing in my view was the place behind the saddle. I said: I will surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and guard him this night until morning. I set out threading through the saddles until I reached the saddle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was not in his saddle. I set out threading through the saddles until I left the camp, and there I saw a dark shape; I headed to it, and it was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Muadh ibn Jabal. They said to me: What brought you out? I said: What brought you two out. Then we saw a thicket not far from us, so we walked to it, and we heard in it like the humming of bees or the rustling of winds. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah here? We said: Yes. He said: And Muadh ibn Jabal? We said: Yes. He said: And Awf ibn Malik? We said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us; we stood asking him nothing, and he asked us nothing. He returned to his saddle and said: Shall I not inform you of what my Lord gave me choice of just now? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He gave me choice between admitting a third of my nation to Paradise without reckoning nor punishment, and intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, which did you choose? He said: I chose intercession. We all said: O Messenger of Allah, make us among the people of your intercession. He said to us: My intercession is for every Muslim."
"16227","Habib ibn Ubayd al-Rahabi from Awf 108 - Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud: Asad ibn Musa told us. And narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir al-Nahwi al-Suri. And narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, they said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi told us, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, from Ismah ibn Rashid al-Umluki and Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd al-Rahabi, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us over the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and I heard him say: O Allah, bless him and forgive him, have mercy on him and grant him health, pardon him, honor his lodging and his return, wash him with water, snow and hail, cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt, replace for him a house better than his house and a family better than his family, protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. Awf said: I saw myself wishing in that standing of mine that I were the deceased in place of that Ansari, for what I saw of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16228","109 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti: Abu al-Mughirah told us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam told us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, that Habib ibn Maslamah brought a man who had misappropriated spoils, bound him beside the mosque, and ordered his goods burned. When he prayed he stood among people, praised Allah and extolled Him, mentioned misappropriation and what Allah revealed concerning it. Awf ibn Malik stood and said: O people, beware of sins with no expiation; a man deals in usury, then repents, and Allah turns to him. And Allah Almighty says: {It is not for a prophet to misappropriate; whoever misappropriates will bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection}. And Allah will raise the devourer of usury on the Day of Resurrection mad, throttled."
"16229","110 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, both said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal told us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar told us, Shubah told us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of sins that are not forgiven: misappropriation; whoever misappropriates something will bring it on the Day of Resurrection. And the devourer of usury; whoever devours usury will be raised on the Day of Resurrection mad, staggering. Then he recited: {Those who devour usury do not stand except as stands one whom Satan prostrates by touch}."
"16230","Ata al-Khurasani from Awf ibn Malik 111 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi told us, Waqid ibn Sulayman told us, Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani told us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat in the last ten of Ramadan. When it was the night of twenty-three he said: Whoever loves to stand with us this night, let him stand my standing, until a third of the night passed. Then he left, and I walked with him to Qutaybah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you stood with us this night? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices a man to stand with the imam until he leaves; a night standing is counted for him."
"16231","Yazid ibn Himyar from Awf ibn Malik 112 - Narrated Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi: Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us, my father told me, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, who said: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Storytellers are three: a commander, one commanded, or an arrogant pretender."
"16232","Asim ibn Humayd from Awf ibn Malik 113 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, that he heard Asim ibn Humayd say: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night. He began and used the tooth-stick, then performed ablution, then stood and prayed; I stood with him. He began and opened with al-Baqarah, not passing a verse of mercy but stopping and asking, nor passing a verse of punishment but stopping seeking refuge. Then he bowed and remained bowing as long as his standing, saying in his bowing: Glory be to the Possessor of power, dominion, pride and greatness. Then he recited Aal Imran, then a surah after surah, doing the like of that."
"16233","Dhu Kala from Awf ibn Malik. 114 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told me. And narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told us, from Azhar ibn Said al-Kalai, from Dhu Kala, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Storytellers are three: a commander, one commanded, or an arrogant pretender."
"16234","Muslim ibn Qarazah al-Ashari from Awf ibn Malik 115 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, that Rabiah ibn Yazid told him, from Muslim ibn Qarazah al-Ashari, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you and the best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you; and the worst of you and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you curse them and they curse you. They said: Shall we not oppose them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, so long as they establish the five prayers. Except one whose governor he oversees and sees him commit something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he commits of disobedience to Allah; and do not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"16235","116 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh told us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from al-Awzai, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Ruzayq ibn Hayyan, from Muslim ibn Qarazah, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and you supplicate to Allah for them and they supplicate to Allah for you; and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you curse them and they curse you. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not oppose them? He said: No, so long as they establish prayer among you. When you see something you dislike from your governor, hate his deed, and do not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"16236","117 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi: Hibban ibn Musa told us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak told us. And narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi: Hisham ibn Ammar told us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir told us, Ruzayq freedman of Banu Fazarah told me, from Muslim ibn Qarazah, who said: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you; and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you curse them and they curse you. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not oppose them then? He said: No, so long as they establish prayer among you. Whoever has a governor over him and sees from him something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he commits of disobedience to Allah, and not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"16237","Abu Ubaydullah ibn Mishkam from Awf 118 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: Abu Mushir and Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri told us. And narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi: Hisham ibn Uthman told us. And narrated Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad: al-Hakam ibn Musa told us, they said: Yahya ibn Hamzah told us, from Yazid ibn Abidah, Abu Ubaydullah told me, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Dreams are three: among them frights from Satan to grieve the son of Adam; among them what a man concerns himself with in wakefulness and sees in his sleep; and among them a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. I said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16238","Damrah ibn Habib from Awf ibn Malik 119 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi: Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi told us, Abu Haywah Shurayh ibn Zayd told us, Abu Adi Artaah ibn al-Mundhir told me, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Awf, count six before the Hour, the first of them my death, then the next its conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, then the next a dwelling your nation settles of Syria in which a pestilence destroys them like the throat-disease of sheep, then the next wealth flowing among you until a man is given a hundred dinars yet remains dissatisfied with it, then the next a tribulation falling among you leaving no Arab house but entering it, then the next Banu al-Asfar making peace with you, gathering at its end with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"16239","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Awf ibn Malik. 120 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri told us, Amr ibn Waqid told us, from Yazid ibn Abi Malik, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: When Egypt was conquered, they reviled the people of Syria. Awf ibn Malik put his head out of a shield and said: O people of Egypt, I am Awf ibn Malik; do not revile the people of Syria, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among them are the Abdal, through them you are aided, and through them you are provided."
"16240","Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani from Awf 121 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi: Hisham ibn Ammar told us, Muhammad ibn Himyar told us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah told us, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani, from Awf ibn Malik, that he entered the mosque leaning upon Dhu Kala, while Kab was storytelling to people. Awf said to Dhu Kala: Will you not forbid this son of your brother from what he does, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None should tell stories to people except a commander, one commanded, or an arrogant pretender."
"16241","Abdullah ibn al-Daylami from Awf ibn Malik. 122 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zurayq al-Himsi narrated to us; my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Daylami say: Awf ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the expedition of Tabuk while he was in a tent, and he heard the sound of my feet and said: Who is this? I said: Awf ibn Malik. He said: Enter, O Awf. I said: All of me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. So I entered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing ablution thoroughly, and he said: O Awf, six signs before the Hour, count them; the first of them: the death of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - say: one. I said: One, and I was struck with intense grief at that. Then he said: The conquest of Iliya (Jerusalem) - say: two. I said: Two. Then wealth will overflow among you until a man is given one hundred dinars and is angry at it - say: three. I said: Three. Then a plague sent upon you like the qu'as (sudden fatal disease) of sheep - say: four. I said: Four. Then a trial emerging from among you that will hardly leave a Muslim house without entering it - say: five. I said: Five. Then a truce between you and the Romans, who will betray at its end; they will gather against you for the period of a woman's pregnancy and come to you with eighty banners, under each banner eighty thousand."
"16242","Shammar Abu Ablah al-Uqayli from Awf ibn Malik. 123 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there will be deceitful years in which the trustworthy will be accused, the treacherous will be trusted, the truthful will be called a liar, the liar will be believed, and al-Ruwaybidah will speak about the affairs of the people. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Ruwaybidah? He said: The foolish man who speaks about the affairs of the public."
"16243","124 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"16244","125 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Dajjal there will be deceitful years in which rain will be abundant and vegetation scarce; the truthful will be called a liar and the liar believed; the treacherous will be trusted and the trustworthy declared treacherous; and al-Ruwaybidah will speak. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Ruwaybidah? He said: One who is not regarded as worth attention."
"16245","Salim ibn Amir al-Khabairi from Awf ibn Malik. 126 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us; Ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir say: I heard Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai say: We stopped with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a halting place, and I woke up at night and saw nothing in the camp taller than the back of a saddle, every man and his camel clinging to the ground. I got up moving through the people until I reached the sleeping place of the Prophet, and he was not in it; I placed my hand on the bedding and it was cold. So I went out moving through the people saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been taken away, until I left the whole camp. I saw a dark figure and went toward it, threw a stone, then went to the dark figure, and there were Muadh ibn Jabal and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah; before us was a sound like the rumbling of a millstone and like the sound of a staff which the winds bend. Some of us said to others: O people, stand still until you wake up or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes to you. We stayed as long as Allah willed, then he called out: Is Muadh ibn Jabal, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and Awf ibn Malik there? We said: Yes. He came toward us until we were with him, neither asking him anything nor he telling us, until he sat on his bedding and said: Do you know what my Lord gave me choice of tonight? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He gave me choice between admitting half my ummah into Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among its people. He said: It is for every Muslim."
"16246","Yahya ibn Jabir al-Tai from Awf. 127 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us; Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from greed that leads to miserliness, and from greed toward that in which there is no hope of attainment."
"16247","128 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us; they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seek refuge with Allah from greed that leads to miserliness, from a coveted thing that returns to greed, and from greed toward that in which there is no hope of attainment."
"16248","Rashid ibn Sad from Awf ibn Malik. 129 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ashath al-Sijzi narrated to us; they said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us. And Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Jurjusi narrated to us; they said: Abbad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews split into seventy-one sects, the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, my ummah will split into seventy-three sects, one in Paradise and seventy-two in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which is it? He said: The Jamaah (the united community)."
"16249","Rabiah ibn Laqit from Awf ibn Malik. 130 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us; Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Rabiah ibn Laqit, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with six or seven or eight men, and he said: Pledge allegiance to me. So we pledged allegiance to him, and he took from us what he took from women, then he followed that with a brief word and said: Do not ask people for anything."
"16250","Rabiah ibn Hudayr from Awf ibn Malik. 131 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us; Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us; they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Rabiah ibn Hudayr, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: We campaigned with Amr ibn al-As, and with us were Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah; severe hunger struck us, and I found people wanting to slaughter a camel, so I said: Shall I help you with it and slaughter it, and you cut me a portion of it? They said: Yes. I did so, then I mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: You have hastened its reward, and I shall not eat it; Abu Ubaydah said the same. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came forward past me, and when he saw me he said: O owner of the camel."
"16251","Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Awf ibn Malik. 132 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Abu Mushir narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; they said: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Busr ibn Abd Allah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish I shall inform you about leadership and what it is: its beginning is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who acts justly."
"16252","Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali from Awf ibn Malik. 133 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us; Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his expeditions; one night I woke up and did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his place, and his Companions were as if rocks were upon their heads, and the camels had laid down their necks. I saw a figure coming toward me, and I approached it, and it was Muadh ibn Jabal. I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Behind me. Then I saw another figure coming toward me, and I approached it, and it was Abu Musa al-Ashari. Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: I heard behind Abu Musa a rumbling like the rumbling of a millstone, so I said: Where is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Behind me, he has come. Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: O Messenger of Allah, when a Prophet is in enemy land he has a guard over him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A comer came to me from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and gave me choice between admitting half my ummah into Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. Muadh said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, you know my kinship and station, so make me among them. He said: You are among them. Awf and Abu Musa said: O Messenger of Allah, you know that we left our families preferring Allah and His Messenger, so make us among them. He said: It is for every Muslim; you two are among them. We reached the people when they called out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit down. They sat as if no one had stood. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A comer came to me from my Lord and gave me choice between admitting half my ummah and intercession, so I chose intercession. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, make us among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be silent. They fell silent as if no one had spoken. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah."
"16253","134 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us. And al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us; they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a night halt with us one night, and each of us spread the foreleg of his mount; I woke up part of the night, and the Prophet's camel was there with no one in front of it. I went out seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there were Muadh ibn Jabal and Abd Allah ibn Qays standing. I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley like the rumbling of a millstone. Only a short while passed until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: A comer came to me from my Lord and gave me choice between admitting half my ummah into Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and companionship to make us among the people of intercession. He said: You are among the people of my intercession. We went together racing to the people, and the people were alarmed, missing their Prophet. He said: A comer came to me from my Lord and gave me choice between admitting half my ummah into Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we beseech you by Allah and companionship to make us among the people of your intercession. When they crowded, he said: I call you to witness that my intercession is for whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah."
"16254","Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from Awf ibn Malik. 135 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Shair narrated to us; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Malih narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Abi al-Malih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Burdah, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My intercession is for whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah."
"16255","Abu Qilabah from Awf ibn Malik. 136 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah and Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilabah, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; we stopped one night, and I got up seeking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not find him; I found Muadh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa al-Ashari, and they said: What do you need? I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: We do not know. While we were thus, we heard at the top of the valley a rumbling like the rumbling of a millstone; soon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we missed you tonight. He said: A comer came to me from my Lord and gave me choice between my ummah being half the people of Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among the people of intercession. He said: O Allah, make us among its people. Then we came to the people and informed them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among the people of your intercession. He said: O Allah, make them among its people. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah."
"16256","137 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us; Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"16257","138 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah."
"16258","Sayf from Ikrimah (Awf). 139 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us; Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, that Sayf narrated to them that Awf ibn Malik narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged between two men, and the one against whom judgment was given said: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring the man back to me. He said: What did you say? He informed him, and he said: Allah blames for helplessness, but you must be resolute; when a matter overcomes you, say: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs."
"16259","al-Azraq ibn Qays from Awf ibn Malik. 140 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us; Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Awf ibn Malik, that he came upon Kab while he was preaching, and said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None should preach except a commander, or one commanded, or one who affects it. So he refrained from preaching until Muawiyah ordered him to do so."
"16260","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi from Awf ibn Malik. 141 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites a letter of the Quran, a good deed is written for him. I do not say to you: Alif Lam Mim, That is the Book; rather alif, lam, mim, dhal, and kaf (each counts separately)."
"16261","142 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"16262","143 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise. He used to ask Allah to move him away from the Fire and did not ask for Paradise; when the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, and he remains in between, he will say: O my Lord, why am I here? He will say: This is what you used to ask Me, O son of Adam. He will say: Yes, O my Lord. While thus, a tree will appear to him at the gate of Paradise extending into Paradise, and he will say: O my Lord, bring me near this tree so I may eat of its fruit and shade myself in its shade. He will say: O son of Adam, did you not used to ask Me? He will say: O my Lord, who is like You? He will keep seeing something better than another and asking, until it is said to him: Go, yours is what your feet have covered and what your eyes have seen. He will strive until exhausted, gesturing with his hand, saying: This and this; and it will be said: This is yours and its like with it. He will be pleased, until he is given what no one of the people of Paradise was given, and he will say: If I were permitted I would feed the people of Paradise food and drink and clothing from what Allah gave me, and nothing of mine would decrease."
"16263","Ibn Samaah from Awf ibn Malik. 144 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us; Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Samaah, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For one's belly to be filled from his pubic region to his throat with pus churning is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"16264","Abd Allah ibn Yazid, storyteller of Maslamah ibn Abd al-Malik, from Awf ibn Malik. 145 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us; Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj and Yazid ibn Husayfah, that they both narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Yazid, storyteller of Maslamah, narrated to them that Awf ibn Malik said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None should preach to people except a commander, or one commanded, or an arrogant pretender."
"16265","Yazid ibn Marthad from Awf. 146 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Jurjusi narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Bashir ibn Talhah narrated to us; Khalid ibn Durayk narrated to me; Yala ibn Munabbih narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on a detachment, and a man said: I shall go out with you provided you assign me a share of the spoils. Then he said: By Allah, I do not know whether you will gain spoils or not, but assign me something fixed. So I assigned him three dinars. We campaigned and gained spoils, and I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I find for him in this world and the Hereafter nothing but these three dinars of his which he took."
"16266","147 - Abu Zurah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Marthad al-Muwaddii, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"16267","Ali al-Uqayli from Awf ibn Malik. 148 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us; Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us at Safa, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali al-Uqayli, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to him: Hold six signs before the Hour - the hadith in full."
"16268","al-Zuhri from Awf ibn Malik. 149 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us; Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Shihab; Awf ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My ummah is three thirds: a third will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment; a third will be given an easy reckoning then enter Paradise; and a third will be sifted and exposed. Then the angels will come and say: We found them saying: There is no god but Allah alone. And Allah will say: They spoke truth; there is no god but Me. Admit them into Paradise for saying: There is no god but Allah alone, and lay their sins upon the people of denial. That is what Allah the Exalted said: And they shall bear their burdens and burdens with their burdens. Its confirmation is in the verse in which He mentioned the angels; Allah Mighty and Majestic said: Then We gave the Book as inheritance to those We chose of Our servants. So He made them three groups, all of them kinds: Among them is one wronging himself - that is the one exposed and sifted; and among them is the moderate - he is the one given an easy reckoning; and among them is the foremost in good deeds by Allah's leave - that is the one who enters Paradise without reckoning or punishment, by Allah's leave. They all enter it together, not separated: They shall be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their garments therein silk; and they shall say: Praise be to Allah who removed grief from us; our Lord is Forgiving, Appreciative; who settled us in the abode of eternity of His bounty; no toil touches us therein nor any fatigue touches us; and those who disbelieve, for them is the Fire of Hell, no decree of death upon them so they die, nor is its punishment lightened for them; thus We recompense every ungrateful."
"16269","Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad from Awf ibn Malik. 150 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a tent of his and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I enter? He said: Enter. I said: All of me? He said: All of you. He said: Hold six that will be before the Hour, the first of them the death of your Prophet - so I wept - then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, a trial entering every house of hair and mud-brick, wealth overflowing among you until a man is given one hundred dinars and is angry at it, a plague among people like the qu'as of sheep, and a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar (Romans) who will betray you and march against you with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"16270","Awf ibn al-Qaqa ibn Mabad ibn Zurarah ibn Urs ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Darim. 151 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Ahmad ibn Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Tawbah ibn Qays ibn Awf ibn al-Qaqa ibn Mabad ibn Zurarah ibn Urs ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Darim narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from my grandfather Awf ibn al-Qaqa, he said: My father came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a young boy with him; he ordered two cloaks for each man and ordered one cloak for me. When we left, one of them sold me one of his two cloaks, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two cloaks. He looked at me and said: Where did you get this? I said: I bought it from so-and-so. He said: You were more deserving of it than him, since he wasted what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him."
"16271","Awf Abu Salamah al-Ansari. 152 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us; my father narrated to me. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah informed us, from Awf ibn Salamah ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the grandchildren of the Ansar, and the freedmen of the Ansar."
"16272","Ikrash ibn Dhuayb al-Tamimi accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him; he is Ikrash ibn Dhuayb ibn Urqus ibn Jadah ibn Amr ibn al-Nazzal ibn Murrah ibn Ubayd. 153 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated to me with this lineage, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from al-Waqidi."
"16273","154 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us; al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Suwayyah al-Minqari narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ikrash ibn Dhuayb narrated to me, from his father, he said: Banu Murrah sent me with the charities of their wealth to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to him in Madinah and found him sitting among the Muhajirun and Ansar. I brought camels as if sinews of arta trees. He said: Who is the man? I said: Ikrash ibn Dhuayb. He said: Go up in lineage. I said: Son of Hurqus ibn Jadah ibn Amr ibn al-Nazzal ibn Murrah ibn Ubayd, and these are the charities of Banu Murrah ibn Ubayd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: These are the camels of my people, these are the charities of my people. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be branded with the charity camels brand and joined to them. Then he took my hand and went with me to the house of Umm Salamah and said: Is there any food? We were brought a large bowl of tharid and meat; we ate from it, and I moved my hand about its sides. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized my right hand with his left hand and said: O Ikrash, eat from one place, for it is one food. Then we were brought a tray with different kinds of fresh dates; I ate from before me, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved about the tray. Then he said: O Ikrash, eat from wherever you wish, for it is of different kinds. Then we were brought water; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his hand, wiped his face, forearms, and head with the wetness of his palms, and said: O Ikrash, this is ablution for what fire has touched."
"16274","Anamah al-Juhani. 155 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Rufay ibn Khalid al-Aishi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anamah al-Juhani, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day and a man of the Ansar met him and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what I see on your face grieves me, and what is it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the man's face a while then said: Hunger. The man went out running or almost running until he reached his house and looked for food in it but found nothing. He went out to Banu Qurayzah and hired himself for one date for each bucket he drew, until he collected a handful of dates. Then he returned with the dates until he found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering he had not left, placed them before him, and said: Eat, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where did you get these dates from? He informed him of the story, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I think you love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with truth, you are dearer to me than my self, my child, my family, and my wealth. He said: Then be patient for poverty and prepare a shield for trial; by the One who sent me with truth, they hasten to one who loves me faster than water descends from a mountaintop to its foot."
"16275","Alyaa al-Sulami. 156 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me. And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; they said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to me, from his father, from Alyaa al-Sulami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not come except upon the dregs of people."
"16276","157 - al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi al-Misri narrated to us; Khidr ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from his father, from Alyaa al-Sulami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not come until a man of the freedmen called Jahjah rules over people."
"16277","Akkaf ibn Wadaah al-Hilali. 158 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai al-Qadi narrated to us; Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Ghusayf ibn al-Harith, from Atiyyah ibn Busr al-Mazini, he said: Akkaf ibn Wadaah al-Hilali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Akkaf, do you have a wife? He said: No. He said: Nor a concubine? He said: No. He said: And you are healthy and wealthy? He said: Yes, praise be to Allah. He said: Then you are of the brethren of devils; either you are of the monks of Christians and thus of them, or you are of us, so do as we do, for marriage is of our sunnah. The worst of you are your unmarried, and the meanest of your dead are your unmarried. Do you wrestle with Satan; he has no weapon more effective against the righteous, men and women, than the married - they are the purified, cleared of indecency. Woe to you, O Akkaf, they are the companions of Dawud, the companions of Yusuf, and the companions of Kursuf. Atiyyah said: Who is Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A man among the Children of Israel on a seacoast who fasted by day and stood by night, never tiring of fasting or prayer; then he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty after that for the sake of a woman he loved, abandoning his worship of his Lord Mighty and Majestic; Allah remedied what had passed and turned to him. Woe to you, O Akkaf, marry, for you are of the sinners. Akkaf said: I shall not leave, O Messenger of Allah, until you marry me to whom you wish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married you in Allah's name and blessing to Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyari."
"16278","Abdah ibn Hazn al-Nasri, dispute over his name and companionship, also called al-Suwai. 159 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdah al-Suwai, he said: People clamored near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, if you sent to them one who forbids them this. He said: If I sent to them forbidding them to come to al-Hajun, some of them would come to it even if he had no need of it."
"16279","Utayr al-Udhri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 160 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us; Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Matir, from his father, from Utayr al-Udhri, that he requested a land grant from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Wadi al-Qura, and it is called today Buwayrat Utayr. He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stopped at Tabuk, praying in Wadi al-Qura."
"16280","Antarah Abu Harun. 161 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us; they said: Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us; al-Mushmail ibn Milhan narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antarah informed us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Whom do you count as martyr among you? We said: O Messenger of Allah, one killed in the path of Allah. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; one dying of belly disease is a martyr; one falling from height is a martyr; a woman dying in childbirth is a martyr; the drowned is a martyr. Al-Hulwani added in his hadith: The consumptive is a martyr, the burnt is a martyr, and the stranger is a martyr."
"16281","Ala ibn al-Hadrami, of his reports. 162 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadahn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beginning with himself."
"16282","163 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Ziyad, from Ibn Ishaq: al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami said: The Hadrami was an ally of Harb ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams. Ibn Ishaq said: The name of al-Hadrami is Abd Allah ibn Abbad ibn al-Sadaf; he was called al-Hadrami only because he came from the land of Hadramawt."
"16283","His lineage. 164 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah Mamar ibn al-Muthanna, he said: al-Hadrami Abu al-Ala, his name: Abd Allah ibn Abbad ibn Akbar ibn Rabiah ibn Malik ibn Arif ibn Malik ibn al-Khazraj ibn al-Sadaf. Al-Ala was a governor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over Bahrayn; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while he was over it, and al-Ala died in Bahrayn or returning from it in year twenty-one, also said year fourteen, also said year fifteen."
"16284","165 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us; Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham narrated to us, freedman of Abu Bakrah, he said: My father al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham narrated to us, from al-Miswar ibn Abd Allah al-Bahili, from one of the children of al-Jarud, from al-Jarud, that he took this copy from the copy of the covenant of al-Ala which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him when he sent him to Bahrayn: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a writing from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, the unlettered Prophet, the Qurashi, the Hashimi, the Messenger of Allah and His Prophet to all creation, to al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami and those Muslims with him, a covenant I covenant to them: Fear Allah, O Muslims, as much as you can, for I have sent over you al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami and ordered him to fear Allah alone without partner, to be gentle among you, to conduct himself well among you, and to judge among you and those he meets by what Allah ordered in His Book of justice. I ordered you to obey him when he does that; if he judges justly, distributes equitably, and when asked mercy shows mercy, then hear and obey him, do well in supporting and aiding him, for obedience to him is incumbent upon you, a mighty right whose full measure you cannot grasp. As Allah and His Messenger have over people generally and over you specially an obligatory right in obedience and fulfilling His covenant, likewise Muslims have over their rulers an obligatory right and obedience; in obedience is attainment of all good and safety from all feared evil. I call to witness over whomever I appoint over any affair of Muslims, little or much: they should seek Allah's choice, then employ over them the best among them; if death befalls al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, Khalid ibn al-Walid, the sword of Allah, succeeds al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami among you, so hear and obey him and do well in supporting and obeying him. March with Allah's blessing, aid, victory, right guidance, and success. Whomever you meet, call them to the revealed Book of Allah and the sunnah of His Messenger, declaring lawful what Allah made lawful in His Book and unlawful what Allah made unlawful, to cast off idols, disavow shirk, kufr, and hypocrisy, to disbelieve in worship of tyrants, al-Lat and al-Uzza, to abandon worship of Isa son of Maryam, Uzayr, angels, sun, moon, fires, and everything set up besides Allah, and to disavow what Allah and His Messenger disavow. If they do that and affirm it, they enter guardianship; call them then by what is in Allah's Book revealed with the Trustworthy Spirit upon His chosen of worlds, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the Messenger of Allah and His Prophet, sent as mercy to all worlds, white and black, jinn and men, a Book with explanation of all that was before you and will be after you, a barrier between people. It confirms the Torah, Gospel, and Psalms, informing you of those before you, their answer to messengers, their belief and denial, the fate of the destroyed for sins, the salvation of the saved, as mercy, guidance from error, light from darkness, healing for breasts, perfection of your religion. When you present this and they affirm, they complete guardianship; present Islam: five prayers, zakat, hajj, fasting Ramadan, bath from janabah, purification before prayer, kindness to parents, joining Muslim kinship. If they do that they are Muslims; call them to iman: testimony that none deserves worship but Allah alone without partner, that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, belief in Allah, His angels, Books, messengers, prophets, the Last Day, this Book and what is before it of Torah, Gospel, Psalms, the evidences, death, life, resurrection, reckoning, Paradise and Fire. If they affirm they are believing Muslims. Call them to ihsan: fulfilling trust and covenant, submission to Muslim leaders, wishing for Muslims what one wishes for himself, belief in the Lord's promises and meeting Him, reckoning the soul daily, fulfilling obligations secretly and openly. If they do that they are beneficent believing Muslims. Describe major sins and warn of destruction: shirk which is not forgiven, sorcery, severing kinship, fleeing battle, misappropriation, killing the believer whose recompense is Hell, slandering chaste women, consuming the orphan's wealth, consuming riba against which is war from Allah and His Messenger. If they avoid major sins they are God-fearing. Call them to worship: fasting, standing, humility, bowing, prostration, devotion, praise, tahlil, tasbih, takbir, charity beyond zakat, modesty, supplication, confession of servitude. If they do that they are worshipping. Call them to jihad, explain its virtue and reward; if they volunteer, pledge them to Allah's sunnah and His Messenger's, with Allah's covenant and protection not to break allegiance nor disobey Muslim rulers. If they affirm, pledge them and seek forgiveness for them. When you go to fight in Allah's path, call people to the same Book, Islam, iman, ihsan, taqwa, worship, and migration; whoever follows is a responding believing beneficent God-fearing worshipping emigrant, with what is yours and upon him what is upon you; whoever refuses, fight him until he returns to Allah's command; whoever covenants and is given Allah's protection, fulfill it; whoever fights or plots or gathers against you or deceives, respond likewise without transgression, for whoever defends after wrong, there is no blame on them. Know Allah is with you, seeing your deeds; fear Allah and beware, for this is a trust my Lord entrusted me to convey to His servants as excuse and proof; whoever acts by it is saved, whoever follows it guided, whoever contends with it succeeds, whoever fights with it helped, whoever abandons it strays until he returns. Learn it, give it your ears, retain it in hearts, for it is light of eyes, spring of hearts, healing for breasts. This is the writing of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami when he sent him to Bahrayn to call to Allah Mighty and Majestic and His Messenger, ordering him to call to its lawful, forbid its unlawful, guide to its rectitude, and forbid its error."
"16285","166 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us; Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: When Khalid ibn al-Walid finished Yamamah, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, sent al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami to Bahrayn. Al-Ala was the one the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent to al-Mundhir ibn Sawa al-Abdi, and al-Mundhir embraced Islam, and al-Ala stayed there as governor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Rabi'ah in Bahrayn apostatized among those Arabs who apostatized, except al-Jarud ibn Amr, who remained upon Islam with those of his people who followed him. Rabi'ah gathered in Bahrayn and apostatized, saying: We shall return kingship to the family of al-Mundhir. They spoke to al-Mundhir ibn al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, called al-Arur; afterwards when he embraced Islam he used to say with the sword upon people: I am not al-Arur but al-Maghrur (the deceived). When Rabi'ah gathered in Bahrayn, al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami marched to them, reinforced by Thumamah ibn Uthal al-Hanafi, who had embraced Islam with his people. When al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami was joined by Thumamah ibn Uthal, he marched with those with him of Banu Suhaym until he waded the sea to Rabi'ah. Rabi'ah marched to them and besieged them at Juwatha, a fortress in Bahrayn, until the Muslims nearly perished of hardship. Abd Allah ibn Hadaq al-Amiri said concerning that hardship: Abd Allah ibn Hadaq said: Let me descend from the fortress and bring you news. With Abd Allah ibn Hadaq was a woman of Banu Ijl. He descended from the fortress and they seized him. They said: Of whom are you? He gave his lineage and called out: O Abjarah - and he was among the people. Abjar came and recognized him. He said: What is your case? He said: I have perished of hunger, so he fed and watered him, and said: Carry me and let me go free. He carried him on a mule and said: Go your way. When Abd Allah ibn Hadaq left them he returned to his companions and informed them that the people were drunk with no strength. Al-Ala with the Muslims of Arabs and non-Arabs attacked them by night, killed them severely, and they fled."
"16286","167 - al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam al-Zafaran narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ibrahim, companion of al-Harawi, narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Abu Kab, companion of al-Harir, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami to Bahrayn, I followed him and saw three traits of him, I know not which of them is most wondrous. We reached the seashore, and they said: Name Allah and plunge in. We named and plunged, crossed, and the water only wet the lower parts of our camels' hooves. When we returned we were in a desert land with no water, so we complained to him; he prayed two rakahs then supplicated, and a cloud like a shield appeared then let down its waterspouts, so we drank and drew water. He died after Abu Bakr sent him to Bahrayn when Rabi'ah apostatized; Allah gave him victory over them and they gave what they had withheld of zakat. He died and we buried him in sand; when we had gone a short distance we said: A beast will come and eat him, so we returned and did not see him."
"16287","168 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: Abu Bakr sent al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami with an army of Muslims toward the people of Bahrayn, who had withheld jizyah; Abu Bakr sent to them when they withheld Allah's right in their wealth. He marched to them with the sea between him and them until they walked in it on their feet, crossing thus a place where ships used to sail before and sail today; he fought them and Allah gave him victory over them, so they submitted, but refused Allah's right in their wealth."
"16288","What al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami transmitted with isnad. 169 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed us; Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Said informed me that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that al-Saib ibn Yazid informed him that he heard al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The emigrant stays in Makkah after completing his rites three days."
"16289","170 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The emigrant stays after completing his rites three days."
"16290","171 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, he said: I heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ask his companions while he was governor of Madinah: What have you heard about staying in Makkah? Al-Saib ibn Yazid said to him: al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The emigrant stays after completing his rites three days."
"16291","172 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us; Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the emigrant, three days."
"16292","173 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us; Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the emigrant, three days after al-Sadar (departure)."
"16293","174 - Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us; Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah al-Azdi, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Hayyan al-Araj, from al-Ala al-Hadrami, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, writing concerning two partners, one Muslim and the other polytheist: Take from the Muslim a tenth, and from the polytheist jizyah."
"16294","175 - Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us; Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadahn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn al-Ala al-Hadrami, from his father, that he wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beginning with himself."
"16295","al-Ala ibn Kharijah, of the residents of Madinah. 176 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Yala, from al-Ala ibn Kharijah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn of your lineages what you join your kinship with, for joining kinship is love for family, increase for wealth, and delay for lifespan."
"16296","al-Ala ibn Khabbab, of the residents of Kufah. 177 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us; Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aish, from al-Ala ibn Khabbab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this foul tree should not approach our mosque - meaning garlic."
"16297","Those named Afif: Afif ibn al-Harith al-Yamani. 178 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzaz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us; Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us; al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Ghassani, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Afif ibn al-Harith al-Yamani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation innovated after its Prophet a bidah in its religion except it lost in exchange a sunnah."
"16298","Afif ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi. 179 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Ziyadi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Muawiyah ibn al-Furat, freedman of the family of Khalid ibn Asid, narrated to us; Hisham ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saib al-Kalbi narrated to me; Farwah ibn Said ibn Afif ibn Madi Karib informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Imru al-Qays was mentioned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is a man remembered in this world, forgotten in the Hereafter, noble in this world, obscure in the Hereafter; he will come on the Day of Resurrection holding the banner of poets, leading them to the Fire."
"16299","180 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Awf ibn al-Mundhir Abu Ghassan al-Muradi narrated to us; Hisham ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saib al-Kalbi narrated to us; Said ibn Farwah ibn Afif ibn Madi Karib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a delegation from Yemen came and mentioned Imra al-Qays ibn Hujr al-Kindi, mentioning two verses of his poetry with mention of a water-caller of Arab waters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is a man remembered in this world, forgotten in the Hereafter, noble in this world, obscure in the Hereafter; he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the banner of poets, leading them to the Fire."
"16300","181 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari al-Naqid and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; they said: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq; Yahya ibn Abi al-Ashath narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Iyas ibn Afif al-Kindi, from his father, from his grandfather Afif al-Kindi, he said: I was a merchant; by Allah, I was with him (al-Abbas) when a man close to him came out; he looked at the sun, and when he saw it decline he stood to pray. Then a woman came out of that tent from which that man had come out, and stood behind him praying. Then a boy nearing puberty came out of that tent praying. I said to al-Abbas: Who is this? He said: This is Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew. I said: Who is this woman? He said: His wife Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. I said: Who is the youth? He said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, his cousin. I said: What is this he does? He said: He prays, claiming to be a prophet; none followed him in his affair except his wife and this youth, his cousin; he claims treasures of Kisra and Qaysar will be opened to him. Afif later embraced Islam; he was cousin of al-Ashath ibn Qays; he used to regret what he missed of Islam then."
"16301","182 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us; Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to us. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us; Said ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khayyat al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Rushd ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us; my uncle Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Asad ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali, from Yahya ibn Afif, from his father, from his grandfather, who was brother of Ibn al-Ashath ibn Qays by his mother, he said: I came to Makkah to buy perfume for my family, and stayed with al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, a merchant. I was with him after sunrise, looking, when a youth came, glanced at the sky, then turned toward the Kabah. Soon a boy came and stood at his right; soon a woman came and stood behind them. The youth said takbir and they said takbir; he bowed and they bowed; he prostrated and they prostrated. I said: O Abbas, a great matter. Abbas said: A great matter; do you know the youth? I said: No. He said: He is Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew. Do you know the woman? I said: No. He said: This is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza, chief of Quraysh women, wife of my nephew; and this is Ali ibn Abi Talib, my nephew. My nephew claims his Lord, Lord of heaven and earth, ordered him with this religion; by Allah, I know no one on earth's face upon this religion but these three."
"16302","Isa ibn Aqil. 183 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us; al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us; Abu Hammad al-Hanafi al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Isa ibn Aqil, he said: I brought a son of mine to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is his name? I said: So-and-so. He said: Rather Abd al-Rahman."
"16303","Imran ibn Husayn, kunyah Abu Nujayd, of his reports and lineage. 184 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Ubayd, he said: Imran ibn al-Husayn is of Banu Ghadrah ibn Khuzaah."
"16304","185 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Waqidi, he said: Imran ibn Husayn ibn Ubayd ibn Khalaf ibn Abd Nahm ibn Hudhayfah ibn Himyar ibn Ghadrah ibn Hubshah ibn Kab ibn Amr ibn Khuzaah; Imran's kunyah Abu Nujayd; he embraced Islam early, he and his father; he campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in expeditions, remained in his people's land, visiting Madinah often until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died; then he moved to Basrah, settling there until he died, with descendants remaining, and Khalid ibn Taliq ibn Muhammad ibn Imran ibn al-Husayn held judgeship of Basrah. It is said Husayn died Muslim, and it was narrated he died polytheist; the correct is he embraced Islam."
"16305","186 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us; Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Shaybah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that when Husayn embraced Islam, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him a supplication to supplicate with."
"16306","187 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nuaym narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, he said: I came to Basrah, where was Abu Nujayd Imran ibn al-Husayn; Umar ibn al-Khattab had sent him to teach the people of Basrah jurisprudence."
"16307","188 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us; Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn al-Husayn died in year fifty-two."
"16308","189 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, he said: I came to Basrah and entered the mosque, and there was an old man white of head and beard leaning against a pillar with a circle around him narrating to them. I said: Who is this? They said: Imran ibn al-Husayn."
"16309","190 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: No Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who came to Basrah excelled Imran ibn al-Husayn."
"16310","191 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said: None like Imran ibn Husayn settled Basrah."
"16311","192 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us; Abu Khushaynah Hajib ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, that Imran ibn al-Husayn said: I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16312","193 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us; Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us; al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn al-Husayn fell ill with an illness as if recognizing death, and one who visited him said to him: What we see almost prevents us (from visiting). He said: Do not do so, for by Allah, what is dearest to Him is dearest to my Lord."
"16313","194 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Imran ibn Husayn said: Sacrificing a young sheep is dearer to me than sacrificing an old one; Allah is most deserving of richness and generosity."
"16314","195 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us; Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hadiths I heard and memorized; nothing prevents me from narrating them except my companions differ with me therein."
"16315","196 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: When the fitnah erupted, Imran ibn al-Husayn said to Hujayr ibn al-Rabi al-Adawi: Go to your people and forbid them the fitnah. He said: I am immersed among them and not obeyed. He said: Convey from me and forbid them it. He said: And I heard Imran swear by Allah: To be a black Abyssinian slave among pebbles atop a mountain herding them until my term overtakes me is dearer to me than to shoot an arrow in either of the two ranks, whether I hit or miss."
"16316","197 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us; Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us; Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Yasar Abu al-Fadl; al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said: The feeders are gone and the beggars remain; the remindful are gone and the forgotten remain. Al-Hasan said: By Allah, were Imran alive today he would speak more."
"16317","198 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me; my uncle Yahya ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Awn al-Uqayli, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The remindful are gone and the forgotten remain; the feeders are gone and the beggars remain."
"16318","199 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb narrated to us; Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us; Hafs ibn al-Nadr al-Sulami narrated to us, from his mother, daughter of Muhammad ibn Imran, from her mother Maryam bint Farwah, that Imran ibn Husayn, when death approached him, said: When I die, bind a turban over my belly, and when you return, slaughter and feed."
"16319","200 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, he said: I saw Imran ibn Husayn wearing khazz (silk-wool mix)."
"16320","201 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, he said: We accompanied Imran from Kufah to Basrah; no day passed but he recited poetry to us, saying to us therein: In equivocation you have ample avoidance of lying."
"16321","202 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Ata, freedman of Imran ibn Husayn, narrated to us, from his father, that Imran ibn Husayn had a brother killed in Jahiliyyah, so he killed seventy for him."
"16322","203 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us; Imran ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, that the angels used to shake hands with Imran ibn Husayn until he was cauterized."
"16323","204 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, that Imran ibn al-Husayn entered ihram from Basrah; when he came to Umar, who had heard of that, he was harsh to him, saying: People say a man of the Prophet's Companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram from an outlying city."
"16324","205 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: We entered upon Imran ibn Husayn in his severe illness, and a man said to him: I pity you for what I see. He said: O my brother, do not do so, for by Allah, what is dearest to Him is dearest to Allah; He said: Whatever misfortune befalls you is for what your hands earned, and He pardons much. This is what my hands earned; then my Lord's pardon comes after in what remains."
"16325","What Imran ibn al-Husayn al-Khuzai transmitted with isnad: Sabrah ibn Mabad al-Juhani from Imran ibn Husayn. 206 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us; al-Harith ibn Mabad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah ibn Amr ibn Suhar ibn Zayd ibn Juhaynah ibn Qudaah ibn Malik ibn Himyar narrated to us; my uncle Harmalah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Sabrah ibn Mabad, Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A group of diverse people gathered with Muawiyah, and he said: Let each man narrate a virtue of his people. The people narrated until the talk reached a youth of Juhaynah, who narrated a hadith but fell short of completing it. Imran ibn al-Husayn turned to him and said: Narrate with your full mouth, O brother of Juhaynah; I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Juhaynah is of me and I am of them; they anger at my anger and are pleased at my pleasure; I anger at their anger and am pleased at their pleasure; whoever angers them angers me, and whoever angers me angers Allah. Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: You lie; the hadith came only about Quraysh. The people said - (report ends truncated in source)."
"16326","Taliq ibn Imran ibn Husayn from Imran. 207 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Nujayd Imran ibn Khalid ibn Taliq the blind narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw Imran ibn Husayn gazing intently at Ali; it was said to him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Looking at Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, is worship."
"16327","Nujayd ibn Imran ibn al-Husayn from his father. 208 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Muhammad ibn Nujayd ibn Imran ibn al-Husayn narrated to me; my father Muhammad ibn Nujayd narrated to me, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: On the day of the Conquest, Khuzah killed a man of Quraysh called al-Harith. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Did they kill him before the prohibition or after? They said: After. He said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so we paid his blood-money; it was the first blood-money paid in Islam."
"16328","209 - Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us; Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani narrated to us; Muslim ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn Nujayd ibn Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A man of Hudhayl killed a man of Khuzah in Jahiliyyah; the Hudhali was in hiding. On the day of the Conquest when the proclamation appeared, he appeared; a man of Khuzah met him and slaughtered him as a sheep is slaughtered. That was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Did he kill him before the proclamation or after? They said: He killed him after the proclamation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been one to kill a believer for a disbeliever I would have killed him for him, but bring out his blood-money. They brought out his blood-money; it was the first blood-money in Islam."
"16329","Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Imran ibn Husayn; Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from his brother Mutarrif. 210 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to me, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people the weak; I looked into the Fire and saw most of its people women."
"16330","211 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us; Muhammad ibn ... narrated to us, from Abu Masud al-Jurayri, from Ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he said: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to a group of his family in the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it, nor did a verse abrogating it descend until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of the people of Islam will keep fighting for Islam, dominant over those opposing them, until they fight the Dajjal. (Note: isnad contains an illegible name in source: Muhammad ibn ...)."
"16331","212 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to some of his family in the ten days. Ibn Kathir and al-Firyabi did not mention Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah in their hadith; Waki perfected it (by adding Mutarrif)."
"16332","213 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us; Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us; they said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his brother Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to a group of his family in the ten days; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it, nor did a Quran verse descend about it; a man said by his opinion what he wished."
"16333","214 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to a group of his family in the ten days; no abrogating verse descended, nor did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it."
"16334","215 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to a group of his family in the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah; he did not forbid it, nor did (an abrogating verse) descend."
"16335","216 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from his brother Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so never breaks fast perpetually. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16336","217 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us. And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Khalid informed us. And Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us; Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us; Abd al-Ala narrated to us; all from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the hadith of Ibn Ulayyah."
"16337","218 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us; Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so never breaks fast by day. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16338","219 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to him or to a man: Did you fast anything of the month of Shaban? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, fast two days."
"16339","220 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us; Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you fast of the end of this month? I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When you break Ramadan fast, fast two days in place of that day."
"16340","221 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Khalid informed us. And Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us; Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us; Abd al-Ala narrated to us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; all from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"16341","222 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated to us; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us; Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his brother Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to him or to another: Did you fast the end of this month? He said: No. He said: When people break fast, or when you break fast, fast two days."
"16342","223 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us; Yahya Abu Ayyub al-Khaqani narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam, what do you command me? He said: Say: O Allah, I seek Your guidance in my affair, and I seek refuge with You from the evil of my soul."
"16343","224 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Most of the people of the Fire are women."
"16344","225 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us; al-Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Ala, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you fast the end of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, fast two days in its place. I asked a man of his family about whom Abu al-Ala narrates this from, and he said: Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16345","226 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us; Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us; Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said: I would never be cauterized after I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about cauterization."
"16346","227 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so fasts perpetually. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16347","Qatadah ibn Diamah from Mutarrif from Imran. 228 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qatadah informed us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my ummah will keep fighting upon truth, dominant over those opposing them, until the last of them fights the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"16348","229 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, he said: I prayed, I and Imran ibn Husayn, in Kufah behind Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him; he said this takbir when bowing and when prostrating, saying all of it. When we finished, Imran said to me: I have not prayed for a while - or for such - resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah more than this prayer."
"16349","230 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us; Khalid ibn Tahir ibn Nizar narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, he said: I prayed, I and Imran ibn Husayn, behind Ali ibn Abi Talib in Kufah; he said takbir whenever he lowered and raised. When he completed his prayer, Imran said: This is a prayer the like of which I have not prayed since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16350","231 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki narrated to us; Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the tamattu of Hajj."
"16351","232 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah; then no book descended about it, nor did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it; a man said therein by his opinion what he wished."
"16352","233 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri narrated to us; they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Quran descended with it; let a man say by his opinion what he wishes."
"16353","234 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Rushd narrated to us; Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah."
"16354","235 - Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Samarqandi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Ibn Shawdhab narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We performed tamattu of Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it is a verse in Allah's Book which nothing abrogated."
"16355","236 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah; then no book descended about it, nor did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it; a man said therein by his opinion what he wished."
"16356","237 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Said ibn Amir narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We were forbidden cauterization; his belly ached thirty years without cauterizing."
"16357","238 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Shuayb al-Naysaburi narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty brings nothing but good."
"16358","239 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us; Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest dwellers of Paradise are women."
"16359","Hani, nephew of Mutarrif, from Mutarrif. 240 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; Abu Harun al-Ghanawi narrated to us; Hani al-Awar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: O Mutarrif, by Allah, had I wished I could narrate to you hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two days consecutively; then increased slowness about some of that, or dislike of it, held me back: that men of the Prophet's Companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I witnessed as they witnessed and heard as they heard - narrate to us hadiths not as they say; I know they do not fall short of truth - or he said: of good - so I fear it may be made dubious to me as made dubious to them. Sometimes he would say: Had I said I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) such-and-such, I would see I spoke truth; and sometimes he stands and says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said such-and-such."
"16360","241 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from the nephew of Mutarrif, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to a man: Did you fast of the end of this month - meaning Shaban? He said: No. He said: When you break Ramadan fast, fast a day or two days."
"16361","Awn ibn Abd Allah al-Uqayli from Mutarrif. 242 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us; they said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Awn al-Uqayli, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, forgive me what I erred, what I intended, what I concealed, what I declared, and what I was ignorant of."
"16362","Said ibn Abi Khayrah from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn. 243 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us; Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Allaf narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Khayrah, from Mutarrif, that he narrated to him from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Tamattu is in Allah's Book; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it, nor did a prohibition descend about it; a man said therein by his opinion, far-reaching as it reached. The wording is of Arim's hadith; Arim and Khalid ibn Khidash said: Said al-Barrad, he is Ibn Abi Khayrah; Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan said in his hadith: It was not forbidden, without mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16363","Ishaq ibn Suwayd al-Adawi from Mutarrif. 244 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Ashath narrated to us; Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd; Mutarrif narrated to me, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization; we were cauterized and neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16364","al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan from Mutarrif. 245 - Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us. And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Ashath narrated to us; they said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us cauterization; we were cauterized and neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16365","Thabit al-Bunani from Mutarrif from Imran. 246 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to a man: Did you fast anything of the end of Shaban? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, fast two days."
"16366","247 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us; Affan narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization; we were cauterized and neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16367","Hadith of Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi from Mutarrif. 248 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah; Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to me, from Mutarrif, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith by which Allah may benefit you: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah; no Quran descended forbidding it, nor did he forbid it until he died; a man said by his opinion what he wished."
"16368","249 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah; he mentioned the same."
"16369","250 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us; Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us; Waki narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Mutarrif, from Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave umrah to a group of his family in the ten days."
"16370","251 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn; and from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah."
"16371","Muhammad ibn Wasi from Mutarrif. 252 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Muhrimi, Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi, and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi narrated to us; they said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twice; a man said by his opinion what he wished."
"16372","Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Qalus from Mutarrif. 253 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us; they said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman, keeper of al-Kira, narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Madan, from Imran ibn al-Qasir, from Abd Allah ibn al-Qalus, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, truthfully from his heart - gesturing with his hand to the skin of his chest - Allah forbids his flesh to the Fire."
"16373","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muwarriq al-Ijli from Mutarrif. 254 - Muhammad ibn Hammuyah al-Jawhari al-Ahwazi narrated to us; Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Alawi narrated to us; Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us; Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muwarriq, from Ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of Allah's servants on the Day of Resurrection are the much-praising; then a group of my ummah will keep fighting those opposing them of the people of shirk until they fight the Dajjal."
"16374","Khalid ibn al-Durayk from Mutarrif. 255 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us; al-Awzai narrated to us; Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Durayk, that Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: I shall narrate to you a hadith: if I recover from this illness, do not narrate it; if I pass my way, narrate it if you wish or leave it. We enjoyed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not forbid us until he died; so a man holds his opinion."
"16375","Kathir Abu al-Fadl from Mutarrif. 256 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us; Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us; Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us; Kathir Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We used to count the false oath (al-yamin al-ghamus) among major sins."
"16376","Ghaylan ibn Jarir al-Maghuli from Mutarrif. 257 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, he said: I prayed behind Ali ibn Abi Talib, I and Imran ibn al-Husayn; when he prostrated he said takbir, when he raised his head he said takbir, and when he rose from two rakahs he said takbir. When he completed prayer, Imran ibn Husayn took my hand and said: This has reminded me of the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); this has prayed with us the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16377","258 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us. And Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us; al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us; they said: Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif, he said: I prayed, I and Imran ibn Husayn, behind Ali ibn Abi Talib; he said takbir when prostrating and when raising his head from prostration. When we finished, Imran, holding my hand, said to me: This man prayed with us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16378","259 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us; al-Walid narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, he said: I prayed, I and Imran ibn Husayn, with Ali ibn Abi Talib; he said takbir when prostrating and when raising his head. When he finished, Imran ibn Husayn said: He prayed with us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16379","260 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us; Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us. And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us; Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us; they said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us; Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to a man: Did you fast the end of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, fast two days."
"16380","Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd al-Dubai from Mutarrif. 261 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization; I was cauterized and neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16381","262 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us; Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Mutarrif narrate, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest dwellers of Paradise are women."
"16382","263 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us; Uthman ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest dwellers of Paradise are women."
"16383","264 - Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest dwellers of Paradise are women."
"16384","Yazid al-Rishk from Mutarrif. 265 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us. And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us. And Bishr ibn Musa and al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Adani narrated to us; they said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and appointed Ali over them; Ali proceeded with the detachment and took a slave girl. They disapproved of that of him, so four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged together, saying: When we meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we shall inform him of what he did. Imran said: Muslims, when they returned from travel, began with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), greeted him, then left. When the detachment returned, they greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of the four stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Ali did such-and-such? He turned away from him. Then another stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Ali did such-and-such? He turned away from him. Then another of them stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Ali did such-and-such? He turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Ali did such-and-such? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him with anger known in his face and said: What do you want of Ali? - three times - Ali is of me and I am of him, and he is guardian of every believer after me."
"16385","266 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us; Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise distinguished from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then for what do workers work? He said: Each is facilitated to what he was created for."
"16386","267 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us; and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known apart from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do workers work? He said: Act, for each one is facilitated toward what he was created for."
"16387","268 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, Sulayman ibn Hasan al-Attar and Hakim ibn Yahya al-Mattuthi narrated to us; they said: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh informed us, my father narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif ibn Abdillah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known apart from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do workers work? He said: Each one is facilitated toward what he was created for."
"16388","269 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known apart from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do workers work? He said: Each one is facilitated toward what he was created for."
"16389","270 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us; both said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known apart from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why the deeds? He said: Act, for each one is facilitated toward what he was created for, according to the decree."
"16390","271 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, who said: Imran ibn Husayn was asked about a man who divorced his wife once without witnesses, then took her back without witnesses. Imran said: You divorced contrary to the Sunnah and took back contrary to the Sunnah; call witnesses to her divorce and to her return."
"16391","272 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakkam narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he was asked, and it was said: Are the people of Paradise distinguished from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He was told: Then why do workers work? He said: Each one works for what he was created for, or for what was facilitated for him."
"16392","273 - Darran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd al-Iyadi narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, why do workers work - for what has already passed, or for what they are yet to face? He said: For what has already passed. He said: Then why do they work? He said: Each one is facilitated."
"16393","274 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami al-Hudhali narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known apart from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. It was said: Then why do workers work? He said: Act, for each one is facilitated toward what he was created for."
"16394","Report of Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Imran ibn Husayn; Qatadah from Abu Raja. 275 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Raja, who said: Imran ibn Husayn came to his wife from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: Tell us what you heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say. He said: This is no time for talk, but she insisted until he spoke, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"16395","Report of Awf from Abu Raja. 276 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu Raja; Imran ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, saying: We were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we travelled by night until, near the end of the night just before dawn, we fell into that deep sleep - and there is no sleep sweeter to the traveller than it - and nothing woke us but the heat of the sun. The first to wake was Bilal, then so-and-so and so-and-so, naming them, then Umar ibn al-Khattab. Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, no one would wake him until he woke himself, for we did not know what might come to him in his sleep. When Umar woke and saw what had befallen the people - and he was a strong man - he said the takbir and raised his voice with it, and kept raising the takbir until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke at his voice. The people complained to him of what had befallen them. He said: No harm; move on. So he moved on and travelled a short distance, then stopped and called for water for ablution and performed ablution, then the call to prayer was made and he led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer, there was a man standing apart who had not prayed with the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What kept you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of major impurity with no water. He said: Use the earth, for it suffices you. Then he travelled on, and the people complained to him of thirst. He stopped and called so-and-so - Abu Raja named him - and called Ali, and said to them: Go and seek water. They went and met a woman with two large waterskins of water on her camel. They said to her: Give us the water. She said: My last contact with water was yesterday at this very hour. They said to her: Then come along. She said: Where to? They said: To the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: The one called the Sabian? They said: He is the one you mean, so come along. They brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what happened. They made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel and placed in it the mouths of the two skins, then rinsed his mouth and returned it into the vessel, then returned it into the mouths of the skins, then tied their mouths, opened the spouts, and called out to the people: Give drink and take water. Whoever wished drank and whoever wished drew water. The last of that was that he gave water to the one who had been in major impurity, saying: Go and pour it over yourself. She stood watching what was done with her water, and by Allah, when they mounted her again after finishing, it seemed to us that the two skins were fuller than before. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather for her dates, barley meal and flour, until they gathered food for her in a garment, loaded her onto her camel and placed it before her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Know, by Allah, that we did not diminish your water at all; rather, it is Allah who gave us drink. She came to her family, having been delayed from them, and they said: O so-and-so, what delayed you? She said: Something amazing - two men met me and took me to this one called the Sabian, and such-and-such happened; by Allah, he is either the greatest sorcerer between these two horizons, or he is truly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Muslims would raid the idolaters around her but would not touch the clan next to her. One day she said to her people: By Allah, I see these people leave us alone; will you not enter Islam? They obeyed her, and they all entered Islam."
"16396","277 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Awf, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey with his Companions when thirst struck them, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16397","278 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor."
"16398","279 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray and Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us; both said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, without doubt."
"16399","280 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. He returned the greeting, then the man sat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He returned the greeting, then he sat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twenty. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He returned the greeting, and said: Thirty."
"16400","Report of Fudayl ibn Fadalah from Abu Raja. 281 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Fadalah; Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to us, saying: Imran ibn al-Husayn came out to us wearing a cloak of khazz (silk-wool blend) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see the trace of His blessing upon him."
"16401","Report of Ismail ibn Muslim from Abu Raja. 282 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a man of the people became ritually impure and found no water, so he performed tayammum and prayed. Then he came upon water during the time of that same prayer, and the man performed ghusl, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not order him to repeat it."
"16402","Report of Imran ibn Muslim al-Qasir from Abu Raja from Imran. 283 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Imran ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Raja, who said: Imran ibn Husayn said: The verse of mutah was revealed in the Book of Allah - meaning the mutah of Hajj - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded it; no verse abrogating the verse of the mutah of Hajj was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it until he died. Then a man said by his own opinion whatever he wished."
"16403","284 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Imran narrated to us; Abu Raja narrated to me, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People will come out of the Fire through the intercession of the intercessors and enter Paradise, and they will be called the Jahannamiyyun (the Hell-dwellers)."
"16404","285 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they travelled late into their night, and he mentioned the hadith in abbreviated form."
"16405","Report of Abdullah al-Luqayti from Abu Raja. 286 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yasin ibn Hammad al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Bahr ibn Kunayz al-Saqqa narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Luqayti, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling weapons during civil strife."
"16406","Report of al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan from Abu Raja. 287 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan; Abu Raja narrated to us, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People will come out of the Fire through the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and enter Paradise; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun."
"16407","288 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will bring out, through my intercession on the Day of Resurrection, people from the Fire who will be called the Jahannamiyyun."
"16408","Report of Salm ibn Zarir from Abu Raja. 289 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us; and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us; both said: Salm ibn Zarir narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Raja; Imran narrated to us that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they travelled late into their night, until near dawn the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted for rest and their eyes overcame them until the sun rose. The first to wake from his sleep was Abu Bakr - and no one would wake the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his sleep until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke himself. Then Umar woke and stood at his head, saying the takbir and raising his voice, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke. When he saw that the sun had risen, he said: Move on. He travelled with us until the sun turned white, then stopped and led us in prayer, while a man of the people stood apart and did not pray with us. When he finished, he said: O so-and-so, what kept you from praying with us? He said: O Messenger of Allah, major impurity befell me. He ordered him to perform tayammum with the earth, then he prayed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me ahead in a mounted party to seek water, for we were seized by severe thirst. While we travelled, we came upon a woman letting her legs hang between two waterskins. We said to her: Where is water? She said: Far, far - no water. We said: How far between you and water? She said: A day and a night. We said: Go with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: What is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We gave her no choice in the matter until we brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We opened the two spouts, and forty thirsty men drank until we were satisfied and filled every skin and vessel with us. Then he said to us: Bring what you have. We gathered for her pieces of bread and dates until we made her a bundle, and he said: Go and feed your family with this, and know that we did not diminish your water at all. When she came to her family, she said: We met either the greatest sorcerer among men, or a prophet as they claim. So Allah guided that clan through that woman, and she accepted Islam and they accepted Islam."
"16409","Report of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Raja from Imran. 290 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Raja, from Imran, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor and needy, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"16410","Report of Amr ibn Abi Ubayd from Abu Raja from Imran. 291 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui al-Qadi narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Musa al-Lului narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill at breakfast or supper until he met Allah, mighty and majestic."
"16411","Report of Abu Nadrah from Abu Raja from Imran. 292 - Abu al-Darda Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us at Tarsus, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Hamzah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Atiq Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and from Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuzai, both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, his sins and wrongs are expiated; when he sets out walking, twenty good deeds are written for him for every step; and when he finishes the prayer, he is rewarded with the deeds of two hundred years."
"16412","What al-Hasan reported from Imran ibn Husayn; Qatadah from al-Hasan from Imran. 293 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Tanukhi narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you say about the adulterer, the thief and the drinker of wine? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They are abominations, and in them there is punishment. Shall I not tell you the greatest of the major sins? Associating partners with Allah. Then he recited: Whoever associates partners with Allah has fabricated a tremendous sin. And disobedience to parents. Then he said: Give thanks to Me and to your parents; to Me is the return. He had been reclining, then sat upright and said: And false speech. And Ibn Abbas said: Everything Allah has forbidden is a major sin."
"16413","294 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; they said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out stoning."
"16414","295 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son's son has died, so what is my share of his inheritance? He said: A sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him and said: The other sixth is an additional allotment."
"16415","296 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We were forbidden from cauterization."
"16416","297 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, but we persisted and were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16417","298 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: And you see people drunk, though they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe."
"16418","299 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."
"16419","300 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah, Yunus and Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife without witnesses and took her back without witnesses. He said: He divorced outside the waiting period and took back contrary to the Sunnah; let him call witnesses now onward."
"16420","301 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves at the time of his death, owning no wealth besides them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16421","302 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, Qatadah and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16422","303 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us; and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed two slaves at his death, owning no wealth besides them, and that was referred to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cast lots among them, freed two of them and returned the rest to slavery."
"16423","304 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah ibn Alqamah al-Bayruti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man of the Ansar freed six persons at his death, owning no wealth besides them, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called for them, cast lots among them, and two were allotted while four were returned to slavery."
"16424","305 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Alqamah ibn Mujashi narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16425","306 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a march, and he had drawn close to his Companions, when he raised his voice with these two verses: O mankind, fear your Lord; indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the Day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nursed, and every pregnant female will deliver her burden, and you will see people drunk though they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe. When the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that, they urged their mounts, knowing he was about to say something. He said: Do you know which day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is the day when Adam will be called; his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire. He will say: O Lord, how many? He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. The people were struck dumb, not a one of them laughed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what was with his Companions, he said: Act and rejoice, for by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that were never in anything but they multiplied it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished of the children of Adam. The distress lifted somewhat from the people. Then he said: Act and rejoice, for by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you among mankind are but like a mole on the flank of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast."
"16426","307 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai; Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while on one of his journeys with the pace among his Companions drawing near, raised his voice with these two verses, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Awanah."
"16427","308 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Tanukhi narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran, who said: When these two verses were revealed to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on one of his marches, with the pace among his Companions drawing close, we held back the mounts, knowing that was upon a statement he would make. When we gathered around him, he said: Do you know which day this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the day when Allah, mighty and majestic, says: O Adam, send forth a delegation to the Fire. He says: O Lord, how many? He says: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine in the Fire. When his Companions heard that, they were struck dumb, and not a man of them showed his teeth. When he saw what was with his Companions, he said: Know and rejoice, for by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, with you are two creations that were never with any people but they multiplied them: Gog and Magog - I think he said - along with those who perished of the offspring of Iblis. And you among mankind are but like a mole on the flank of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast."
"16428","309 - Musa ibn Harun and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us; both said: Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqqashi narrated to us; and Ismail ibn Numayl al-Khallal al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us; both said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn and Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nuh had three sons: Sam, the father of the Arabs; Ham, the father of the Abyssinians; and Japheth, the father of the Romans."
"16429","310 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that Samurah ibn Jundub and Imran ibn Husayn discussed, and Samurah narrated that he remembered from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two pauses: a pause when he said the takbir, and a pause when he finished reciting Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray; and Imran denied it, so they wrote about that to Ubayy ibn Kab, and in his letter to them was that Samurah had remembered correctly."
"16430","311 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated to us, Bahr ibn Kunayz al-Saqqa narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a pause. Samurah said: Two pauses. So they wrote to Ubayy ibn Kab, and he wrote: You remembered correctly, O Samurah, and the people forgot."
"16431","312 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us; both said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not ride on purple-dyed saddles, nor wear saffron-dyed garments or those embroidered with silk."
"16432","313 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Malik ibn Sad al-Qaysi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Garments edged with silk are not to be worn."
"16433","314 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us; both said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The perfume of men is scent without colour, and the perfume of women is colour without scent."
"16434","315 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Amr ibn Humran al-Basri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam, nor janab nor jalab. Shighar is for a man to marry the sister of another while the other marries his sister, without dowry; and jalab and janab were practices in horse-racing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked public wailing for the dead and forbade it, and emphasized it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders spoils is not of us."
"16435","316 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam."
"16436","317 - Ibrahim ibn Mathawayh al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Khalid ibn Nujayh al-Bakri al-Abdi narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of red garments, for it is the adornment most beloved to Satan."
"16437","318 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Bakr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man wearing red garments and said: This is the adornment of Satan."
"16438","319 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the wealth of his brother, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16439","320 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately swears a false oath, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16440","321 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqqashi narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn and Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, then the nearest, the nearest."
"16441","322 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Jarud narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so we were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16442","323 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us cauterization, so we were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16443","Report of Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 324 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd, Habib and Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari over an army, and Imran ibn Husayn met him in the governor's house among the people and said: Do you know why I came to you? Do you remember that when it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what his commander had said to him - Stand and fall into the fire - the man stood to fall in, but was caught and held back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he fallen into it, both would have entered the Fire; there is no obedience in disobedience to Allah? He said: Yes, he said it; and I only intended this hadith."
"16444","325 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us; both said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur, Yunus and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and forbade us mutilation."
"16445","326 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that a man came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: My slave has fled, and I vowed that if Allah returns him, I will cut off his hand. He said: Do not cut off his hand, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command charity and forbid mutilation."
"16446","327 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that a man came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: My slave has fled, and I swore that if I find him I will cut off his hand. He said: Do not cut off his hand, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand among us forbidding us mutilation and commanding charity."
"16447","328 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit and Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn or another, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey when Surah al-Hajj was revealed, and he raised his voice with it while the people had dozed and their mounts had scattered: O mankind, fear your Lord; indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a tremendous thing, up to: but the punishment of Allah is severe. They gathered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), thinking the Hour had come. He said: Do you know which day that day is? They said: Which day is it? He said: It is the day when Allah, mighty and majestic, says: O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire. He says: What is the delegation of the Fire? He says: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one in Paradise. The people were struck dumb, not one of them showing his teeth. He said: Act and rejoice, for no prophethood ever came but ignorance preceded it, so the number is completed from the people of ignorance, and what remains is completed from the hypocrites. And he said: Act and rejoice, for you among mankind are but like a mole on the flank of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast, and you are between two creations that were never in anything but they multiplied it: Gog and Magog, along with those who perished of the offspring of Adam and Iblis."
"16448","329 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us; both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah, Yunus and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, that Imran ibn Husayn was asked about a man who divorced his wife without witnesses and took her back without witnesses. He said: He divorced outside the waiting period and took back contrary to the Sunnah; let him call witnesses from now on."
"16449","330 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so I was cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16450","331 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization."
"16451","332 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; both said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a march when they slept past the dawn prayer and woke at the heat of the sun. They moved a little until the sun rose fully, then he ordered a caller who called the adhan, and he prayed two rakahs before dawn, then the iqamah was made and he prayed the dawn prayer."
"16452","333 - Ubayd ibn Khalaf al-Qatii narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his brother, whose belly was swollen with dropsy. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother's belly is swollen; I took him to physicians, and they ordered cauterization. Shall I cauterize him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not cauterize him, and return him to his family. A camel passed by him and struck his belly, and his belly subsided. He brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had you taken him to physicians, you would have said: The fire healed him."
"16453","334 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man owned six slaves and freed them at his death, owning no wealth besides them. That was referred to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who disapproved of it, divided them into three groups, cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16454","335 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning a man who freed six slaves at his death: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided them and freed a third."
"16455","336 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sariyah al-Akkawi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Said al-Bajali, from Umar ibn al-Subh, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights in the sea in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who is in His path - has rendered to Allah all His obedience, sought Paradise by every seeking, and fled the Fire by every flight."
"16456","337 - Muhammad ibn al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his brother in his absence, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter."
"16457","338 - Muhammad ibn Haywah al-Jawhari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Nahwi al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will emerge from the direction of Isfahan."
"16458","Report of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan from al-Hasan from Imran. 339 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal has indeed eaten food and walked in the markets."
"16459","Report of Thabit al-Bunani from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 340 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: This verse was revealed: O mankind, fear your Lord; indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a tremendous thing, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; some of the people had dozed and some had scattered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his voice with it, so they gathered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Hour has come. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it and said: Do you know which day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is when Allah, mighty and majestic, says to Adam: Rise, O Adam, and send forth the delegation of the Fire. He says: What is the delegation of the Fire? He says: Send from every thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. The people were struck dumb, not one of them showing his teeth. He said: Act and rejoice, for you among mankind are but like a mole on the back of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast. Then he said: Know that you are with two creations that were never in anything but they multiplied it: Gog and Magog, along with those who perished of the offspring of Iblis."
"16460","Report of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Hasan from Imran. 341 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamani narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16461","Report of Khalid al-Hadhdha from al-Hasan. 342 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man freed six slaves of his at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them and freed two of them."
"16462","Report of Ziyad al-Alam from al-Hasan from Imran. 343 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, Attab ibn Harb narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum, from Ziyad al-Alam, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation, saying: Mutilation includes a man vowing to perform Hajj walking conspicuously, on foot; whoever swears anything of that, let him expiate his oath and then ride."
"16463","Report of Said ibn Rashid al-Sammak from al-Hasan from Imran. 344 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Said ibn Rashid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he halted us for rest until the end of the night. We woke with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the sun had risen, and he said: Move on, move on. We moved on until, when the sun was at its zenith, he stopped and ordered Bilal, who called the adhan; each of us prayed two rakahs, then he led us in prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we repeat it tomorrow at its time? He said: Would your Lord forbid you usury yet accept it from you?"
"16464","Report of Kathir ibn Shinzhir from al-Hasan. 345 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation; of mutilation is for a man to slit his nose, and of mutilation is for a man to vow to perform Hajj on foot - if he does that, let him offer a sacrifice and ride."
"16465","Report of Said ibn Zarbi Abu Ubaydah al-Baji from al-Hasan. 346 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Salih ibn Malik al-Khwarizmi narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Baji Said ibn Zarbi narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts for some men of my people. He said: By Allah, I will not mount you; by Allah, I have nothing to mount you upon - twice. Then three loads of the finest camels came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent for us and mounted us. When we had gone on with them, I said to my companions: I do not see blessing in them, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sworn not to mount us, yet he mounted us. We returned to him and told him of his oath. He said: I did not forget my oath; rather, when I swear an oath and see something better than it, I do what is better and expiate my oath."
"16466","347 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, chose this religion for Himself; nothing befits your religion but generosity and good character, so adorn your religion with them."
"16467","Report of Abu Amir al-Khazzaz from al-Hasan from Imran. 348 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a brass ring on his upper arm. He said: What is this? He said: For the wahinah (a pain believed to be warded off by the ring)? He said: Would you like to be entrusted to it? Cast it off from yourself."
"16468","Report of Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik from al-Hasan from Imran. 349 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Malik ibn Sad al-Qaysi narrated to us; and Sahl ibn Musa Shiran narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us; both said: Rawh narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation."
"16469","350 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation."
"16470","351 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves at his death, owning no wealth besides them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16471","352 - Musa ibn Isa al-Jazari al-Basri narrated to us, Suhayb ibn Abbad ibn Suhayb narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us but he commanded us charity and forbade us mutilation."
"16472","Report of Jisr ibn Farqad from al-Hasan from Imran. 353 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Raja al-Abadani narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Jisr ibn Farqad, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Hurayrah, both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about His saying: And pleasant dwellings in the Gardens of Eden. He said: A palace in Paradise of pearl, wherein are seventy houses of red ruby; in each house seventy rooms of green emerald; every room seventy beds; upon every bed seventy beddings of every colour; upon every bedding a wife; in every house seventy tables; upon every table seventy kinds of food; in every house seventy servants, male and female; and the believer will be given strength to partake of all that in a single morning."
"16473","Report of Abu Sahl Muhammad Amr al-Ansari from al-Hasan from Imran. 354 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, my father narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhalhal, from Abu Sahl, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once gathered the Banu Hashim and said to them: O Banu Hashim, I avail you nothing against Allah; O Banu Hashim, my allies among you are the God-fearing; O Banu Hashim, guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date; O Banu Hashim, let me not find you coming with this world carried upon your backs while others come with the Hereafter."
"16474","Report of Ishaq ibn al-Rabi Abu Hamzah al-Attar from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 355 - Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin al-Basri narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Rabi Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he saw a man with a brass ring on his upper arm and said to him: What is this? He said: It was prescribed for me for the wahinah. He said: If you die with it upon you, you will be entrusted to it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who seeks omens or has omens sought for him, who practises soothsaying or has it practised for him - I think he said - or practises magic or has it practised for him."
"16475","356 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us; and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us; both said: Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of the rich is a blemish on his face - if little, then little; if much, then much."
"16476","357 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and returned four to slavery."
"16477","358 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and returned four to slavery."
"16478","359 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and returned four to slavery."
"16479","360 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that a man said to Imran ibn Husayn: A man died in Khurasan and was wailed over in Basra - will he be punished? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth, and you have lied."
"16480","Report of Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari from al-Hasan from Imran. 361 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; and Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to us; both said: Waki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuzai, that a man freed six slaves in his illness, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16481","Report of Abu al-Ashhab Jafar ibn Hayyan from al-Hasan from Imran. 362 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi narrated to us; they said: Waki narrated to us, from Abu al-Ashhab, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of the rich is a blemish on his face."
"16482","Report of Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali from al-Hasan from Imran. 363 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience or anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16483","364 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience or anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16484","Report of Anbasah ibn Abi Raitah al-Ghanawi from al-Hasan from Imran. 365 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Anbasah al-Ghanawi, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six owned slaves of his at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16485","366 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Anbasah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"16486","Report of al-Hasan ibn Dinar from al-Hasan from Imran. 367 - Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli al-Asbahani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Imran ibn Husayn said to al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to Allah? He said: Yes."
"16487","368 - Musa ibn Isa al-Jazari al-Basri narrated to us, Suhayb ibn Abbad ibn Suhayb narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man of the Ansar freed six persons at his death, owning nothing but them, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called for them, cast lots among them, released two and returned four to slavery."
"16488","Report of Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Shanni from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 369 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Shanni narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: While Imran ibn al-Husayn was narrating from our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man said to him: O Abu Nujayd, narrate to us from the Quran. Imran said to him: Do you and your companions read the Quran - could you tell me how much zakat is due on gold, camels, cattle and kinds of wealth, whether you were present or absent? Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed in zakat such-and-such. The man said: O Abu Nujayd, you have revived me; may Allah keep you alive. Then al-Hasan said: That man did not die until he became one of the jurists of the Muslims."
"16489","Report of Hathmah ibn Abi Hathmah from al-Hasan from Imran. 370 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdillah and Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, who said: Imran ibn Husayn and I were in Basra when we passed a blind man reciting Surah Yusuf. We stood listening; when he finished his recitation, he begged. Imran ibn al-Husayn said: We belong to Allah and to Him we return, then said: Move on with me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever recites the Quran, let him ask Allah by it, for after you there will be people who recite the Quran and beg people by it."
"16490","371 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever recites the Quran, let him ask Allah by it, for there will come peoples who recite the Quran and beg people by it."
"16491","372 - Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16492","373 - Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: I found in my grandfather's book, in his handwriting: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Idris al-Kufi, from Mansur, from a man, from al-Hasan, from Imran, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran and ask Allah by it before there come peoples who will beg people by it."
"16493","374 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us; and Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us; both said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he passed a storyteller telling stories; when he finished, he begged. He said: We belong to Allah and to Him we return; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran and ask Allah by it before there come peoples who recite the Quran and beg people by it."
"16494","Report of Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr from al-Hasan from Imran. 375 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep many sandals, for one of you remains as though mounted so long as he wears sandals."
"16495","Report of Hisham ibn Hassan from al-Hasan from Imran. 376 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Mutarrif Abu Sufyan al-Saruji narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade accepting the food of the wicked."
"16496","377 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati and Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us; both said: Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's standing in the rank in the path of Allah is better than sixty years of worship."
"16497","378 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us; and Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us; both said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We travelled by night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted us for rest at the end of the night and woke after the sun had risen. Each of us rushed to his ablution in confusion. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Move on. We moved on until, when the sun had risen high, we stopped, relieved ourselves, performed ablution, then he ordered Bilal, who called the adhan; we prayed two rakahs, then Bilal made the iqamah and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we make it up at its time tomorrow? He said: Does your Lord forbid you usury yet accept it from you?"
"16498","379 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while disliking three tribes: the Banu Umayyah, the Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."
"16499","380 - Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn; and Sahl ibn Musa al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning - they do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. Ukkashah ibn Mihsan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me of them. He said: O Allah, make him of them. Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me of them. He said: Ukkashah beat you to it."
"16500","381 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to the Creator."
"16501","Report of Humayd al-Tawil from al-Hasan from Imran. 382 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam; and whoever plunders spoils is not of us."
"16502","383 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam; and whoever plunders spoils is not of us."
"16503","384 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"16504","385 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, Yunus and Habib, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah."
"16505","386 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us; and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us; both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us with a sermon but he commanded us charity and forbade mutilation."
"16506","387 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Rahhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhammir al-Harrani narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"16507","388 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us but he commanded us charity and forbade us mutilation."
"16508","389 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We practised tamattu during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he did not forbid it to us, nor did Allah, mighty and majestic, reveal anything concerning it."
"16509","Report of Abu Qazaah from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 390 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn al-Harishi al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Fazari narrated to us; both said: Shubah narrated to us, Abu Qazaah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam."
"16510","Report of Mubarak ibn Fadalah from al-Hasan from Imran. 391 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us; they said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on a man's upper arm a ring and said: What is this? He said: For the wahinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will only increase you in weakness; cast it off from yourself - if you die with it upon you, you will be entrusted to it."
"16511","392 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yala ibn Abbad ibn Yala narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us cauterization, so we were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"16512","393 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, owning no wealth besides them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and returned four to slavery."
"16513","Report of Amr ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Imran. 394 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Amr ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals, forty lashes."
"16514","Report of Salm ibn Bashir from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 395 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, from Salm ibn Bashir, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's standing in a rank in the path of Allah is better than this world and what is in it; whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah - whether it hits or misses - it counts as freeing a slave; and whoever grows grey hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"16515","Report of Shabib ibn Abi Shaybah from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 396 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Shabib ibn Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: How many gods do you worship today? He said: Seven - six on earth and one in heaven. He said: Which of them do you count upon for your hope and fear? He said: The One in heaven. He said: O Abu Husayn, if you accept Islam, I will teach you two phrases that will benefit you. When Husayn accepted Islam, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the two phrases you promised me. He said: Say: O Allah, inspire me with my right guidance, and protect me from the evil of my soul."
"16516","397 - Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Shabib ibn Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16517","Report of Ubayd ibn Mihran from al-Hasan. 398 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can none of you do each day deeds like Uhud? They said: O Messenger of Allah, who can do each day deeds like Uhud? He said: Each of you can. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what? He said: Glory be to Allah is greater than Uhud; there is no god but Allah is greater than Uhud; praise be to Allah is greater than Uhud; and Allah is Greatest is greater than Uhud."
"16518","Report of Ismail ibn Muslim al-Makki from al-Hasan from Imran. 399 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: When we slept past the prayer and woke, we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not pray such-and-such prayers? He said: Would our Lord forbid us usury yet accept it from us? Negligence is only in wakefulness."
"16519","400 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman and Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The begging of the rich is a blemish on his face on the Day of Resurrection; the begging of the rich is fire - if given little, then little; if given much, then much."
"16520","401 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam."
"16521","402 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us but he commanded us charity and forbade us mutilation."
"16522","Report of Simak ibn Harb from al-Hasan from Imran. 403 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man owned six slaves and freed them at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16523","404 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves, and his heirs came finding nothing, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. He said: Had I known that, Allah willing, I would not have prayed over him. He cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16524","405 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Misisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us; and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us; both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, and his Bedouin heirs came and told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he had done. He said: Why did he do that? He cast lots among them, so two were freed and four were returned to slavery."
"16525","406 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man freed six boys of his at his death, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached concerning them, so he cast lots among them; two of them were drawn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed the two who were drawn and kept four in slavery."
"16526","407 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Hafs ibn Imran narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to Allah."
"16527","Report of Ata ibn al-Saib from al-Hasan from Imran. 408 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Mahbub ibn Muhriz al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, owning no wealth besides them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16528","Report of Mansur ibn Zadham from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 409 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is of faith, and faith is in Paradise; obscenity is of harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."
"16529","410 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Yunus, Mansur and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, commanding us charity and forbidding us mutilation."
"16530","411 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Imran, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, punishes the dead through the wailing of his family over him. A man said: A man dies in Khurasan and is wailed over here - will he be punished? Imran said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth, and you have lied."
"16531","412 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Umar ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, (H). And Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, (H). And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man from the Ansar freed six slaves of his at the time of his death while he had no wealth other than them, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he became angry at that and said: I had intended not to pray over him, then he summoned his slaves and divided them into three parts, and cast lots among them, and freed two and kept four enslaved."
"16532","413 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (H). And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, both said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a Muslim woman was captured by the enemy, and they had earlier taken a she-camel belonging to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she saw negligence on the part of the people, so she rode the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she vowed to slaughter the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Evil is what you have rewarded her with; there is no vow for the son of Adam regarding what he does not own, nor in disobedience of Allah."
"16533","414 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he saw a brass ring on a man's hand and said: What is this? He said: Against weakness. He said: It will only increase you in weakness, and if you were to die while believing it benefits you, you would die upon other than the fitra."
"16534","415 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."
"16535","Abu Ma'bad from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn. 416 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talha al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu Ma'bad narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be four tribulations: a tribulation in which blood will be made lawful, and the second in which blood and wealth will be made lawful, and the third in which blood, wealth, and private parts will be made lawful."
"16536","Isma'il ibn Ubaydillah ibn Salman al-Makki from al-Hasan from Imran. 417 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hadithi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ubaydillah ibn Salman al-Makki narrated to me, al-Hasan narrated to me, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man's standing in a rank in the path of Allah is better than worship of sixty years."
"16537","Ziyad al-Jassas from al-Hasan from Imran. 418 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Jurjani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ziyad al-Jassas informed us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, wearing a green khazz cloak which Ziyad had given him as a gift, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah the Exalted bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him."
"16538","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn. 419 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A man asked him: A man divorced but did not call witnesses, and took her back but did not call witnesses? He said: Evil is what he did; he divorced in innovation and took her back in other than the Sunna; let him call witnesses to what he did."
"16539","420 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: A man asked Imran ibn Husayn about a man who divorced but did not call witnesses, and took her back but did not call witnesses. He said: He divorced outside the waiting period and took her back outside the Sunna; let him call witnesses to his divorce and to his return, and let him seek Allah's forgiveness."
"16540","421 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that a man asked Imran ibn Husayn: A man divorced but did not call witnesses, and took her back but did not call witnesses? He said: Evil is what he did; he divorced in innovation and took her back in other than the Sunna; let him call witnesses to what he did."
"16541","422 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham and Habib, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, the same."
"16542","423 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Husayn was asked about a man who divorced but did not call witnesses, and took her back but did not call witnesses? He said: He divorced outside the Sunna and took her back outside the waiting period; let him call witnesses now."
"16543","424 - Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn Hubab narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sadaqa, from Muhammad, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It is he who says: Seventy thousand will enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not take evil omens, nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they rely."
"16544","425 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my umma will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment. It was said: Who are they? He said: Those who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqya, nor take evil omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"16545","426 - Ahmad ibn al-Jahm al-Sammari narrated to us, Abu al-Jawza' Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us, (H). And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abu Khayra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my umma will enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqya, nor take evil omens, and upon their Lord they rely. Imran said: We cauterized but we did not prosper nor succeed."
"16546","427 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my umma will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment. It was said: Who are they? He said: They are those who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqya, nor take evil omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"16547","428 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man had six slaves and freed them at his death, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, and freed two and kept four enslaved."
"16548","429 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha' Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man freed six slaves in his illness, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them and freed two and kept four enslaved."
"16549","430 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Fayd ibn Wathiq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq and Ayyub, (H). And Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, the same, except that he added in it: Had it not reached me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it would have been my opinion."
"16550","431 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn. Jarir said: And Ayyub also narrated to me from Abu Qilaba al-Jarmi, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A man from the Ansar died and left six slaves, with no wealth other than them, and he freed them all at his death, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he divided them into three parts, then cast lots among them, and freed a third and kept two thirds enslaved. Muhammad ibn Sirin said: Had this not reached me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that would have been my opinion."
"16551","432 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Salm ibn Abi al-Dhiyal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, that al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari and Imran ibn Husayn, or one of them, and I think it was Imran, used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah. And the other said: Allah is Greatest, three times, or as he said."
"16552","433 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Salama ibn Alqama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah."
"16553","434 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Haydun ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sila ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: al-Hakam al-Ghifari was appointed over Khurasan, and that reached Imran ibn al-Husayn, so he sought al-Hakam until he met him in al-Rahba, and said: I kept seeking you since today; you have been sent over a grave matter. Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah? He said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is Greatest; I thought you had forgotten."
"16554","435 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari and Imran ibn Husayn met, and one of them said to the other: Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience of Allah? He said: Allah is Greatest."
"16555","436 - Abu Ubayda Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he combined Hajj and Umra, and said: We did so with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16556","437 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to a created being in disobedience of Allah."
"16557","438 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah."
"16558","439 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Fadl Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sadaqa, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Imran, say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance to the most rightful of my affairs, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul."
"16559","440 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Subayh say: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin; they mentioned in the presence of Imran ibn Husayn: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living, and they said: How is he punished by the weeping of the living? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said so."
"16560","441 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves the believer when he is poor yet abstinent."
"16561","442 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Matar ibn Muhammad ibn Janah al-Sukkari narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Salim al-Misma'i narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16562","443 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (H). And Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him."
"16563","444 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wars al-Damli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Awn narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man fought another man and bit his hand, and he pulled it away, and his front tooth fell out, and he disputed with him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Would he leave it in your mouth for you to bite it as the stallion bites? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled its blood-money."
"16564","445 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man while lying in it, let him take with his face his seat in the Fire."
"16565","446 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a compelled binding false oath deliberately, let him take with his face his seat in the Fire."
"16566","Abu al-Muhallab Mu'awiya ibn Amr al-Jarmi, uncle of Abu Qilaba, from Imran. Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan from Abu al-Muhallab from Imran. 447 - Abu Ubayda Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Muhammad al-Bunani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Miqsam narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Mu'awiya ibn Amr Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves at his death while he had no wealth other than them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, and kept four enslaved and freed two."
"16567","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu al-Muhallab. 448 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, both said: Bishr ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so stand and pray over him. So we lined up as we line up for the dead, and we prayed over him as we pray over the dead."
"16568","Abu Qilaba from his uncle Abu al-Muhallab from Imran. Ayyub from Abu Qilaba. 449 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A woman cursed a she-camel of hers, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: It is cursed, so leave it alone. He said: I saw it following the dwellings with no one touching it, a grey she-camel."
"16569","450 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (H). And Yusuf the judge and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, both said: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, (H). And Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, he heard a curse and said: What is this? They said: A woman cursed a she-camel of hers. He said: Put down its load, for it is cursed. So they put down its load, and it was a grey she-camel."
"16570","451 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and a woman cursed a she-camel of hers, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw off its saddle from it; it is as if I look at it, a grey she-camel."
"16571","452 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulaya narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys, and a woman from the Ansar was on a she-camel, and it became distressed and she cursed it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and said: Take what is on it and leave it, for it is cursed. Imran said: It is as if I see it wandering in the market with no one touching it, and perhaps he said: in the market of Madina."
"16572","453 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Banu Amir had captured two men from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) captured a man from Thaqif and took his she-camel, on which he used to outrace the pilgrims. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was bound, and he said: O Muhammad, O Muhammad. So he turned to him, and he said: For what am I detained, and the forerunner of the pilgrims taken? He said: For the offense of your allies, and Banu Amir were allies of Thaqif. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on, and he called him again: O Muhammad. He answered him: I am a Muslim. He said: Had you said that while you controlled your affair, you would have attained complete success. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on, and he called him again, so he returned to him, and he said: Feed me, for I am hungry. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is your need. So he ordered food for him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed the man for the two men of his companions who had been captured. And some polytheists raided the outskirts of Madina and took that she-camel, and among what they took they also took a woman, and they took her to their dwellings. The woman rose in part of the night among their camels, and they used to make them kneel in their courtyards, and whenever she approached a camel to ride it, it grumbled, so she left it, until she came to the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a docile she-camel, and it did not grumble until she sat on its rear, then she urged it on, and the people became aware of her, and they rode in pursuit of her. She vowed, while fleeing with them in pursuit, that if Allah saved her on it, she would slaughter it. She escaped, and when she arrived at Madina, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told: This is your she-camel; so-and-so woman came on it, Allah having saved her on it from the polytheists. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought the woman and the she-camel, and he asked her: How did you do it? She told him, and said: And I vowed, while they were pursuing me on it, to slaughter it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil is what you have rewarded her with then; there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, nor in what the son of Adam does not own."
"16573","454 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (H). And Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb and Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The polytheists raided the pastures of Madina and took them, and al-Adba' was among what they took, and they captured a Muslim woman. When night came they would bring their camels back to their courtyards, and one night the woman rose in the night, and they had been put to sleep, and she kept placing her hand on no camel but it grumbled, until she came to al-Adba', a docile, guarded she-camel, and she rode it, and she vowed that if Allah the Exalted saved her on it, she would slaughter it. When she arrived, the she-camel was recognized; it was said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was told of her vow, and he said: Evil is what you have rewarded her with; if Allah saved you on it, you would slaughter it? There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, nor in what the son of Adam does not own."
"16574","455 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us ... Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Banu Uqayl were allies of Thaqif in the Jahiliyya, and they captured two Muslim men, and he mentioned the hadith."
"16575","456 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulaya narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed two Muslim men for a polytheist man from Banu Uqayl whom Thaqif had captured, and Banu Uqayl were allies of Thaqif in the Jahiliyya, and Thaqif had captured two Muslim men, so the Muslims captured a man from Banu Uqayl and took a she-camel of his that had outrun the pilgrims in the Jahiliyya; when a she-camel outran in the Jahiliyya, no water basin it came to was withheld from it, nor any pasture it grazed. The man sat in a place, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him, and he said: O Muhammad, for what am I detained, I and the forerunner of the pilgrims? He said: We detained you for the offense of your allies, Thaqif. And he mentioned the hadith."
"16576","457 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us ... (H). And Yusuf the judge and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves at his death while he had no wealth other than them, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said stern words about the man, and he summoned them and divided them into three parts, and cast lots among them, and freed two and kept four enslaved."
"16577","458 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A man from the Ansar died and left six slaves with no wealth other than them, and he freed them all at his death, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he divided them into three parts, then cast lots among them, and freed a third and kept two thirds enslaved."
"16578","459 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16579","460 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him."
"16580","461 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him, meaning al-Najashi."
"16581","462 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him. So we stood and prayed over him."
"16582","463 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mubashshir al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man says to his brother, O disbeliever, it is like killing him, and cursing the believer is like killing him."
"16583","Khalid al-Hadhdha' from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Muhallab from Imran. 464 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam after three rak'as of Asr, then entered, and a man called al-Khirbaq, who had long hands, stood up to him and said: Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah? So he came out angry, dragging his cloak, and said: Is he truthful? They said: Yes. So he stood and prayed that rak'a."
"16584","465 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr as three rak'as, and a man called al-Khirbaq said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you only prayed three rak'as. He said: Is that so? They said: Yes. So he prayed a rak'a, then recited tashahhud and gave salam, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"16585","466 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) erred in a prayer and prostrated two prostrations in which he gave salam."
"16586","467 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam after three rak'as of Asr, then stood and entered the chamber, and al-Khirbaq, a man with outspread hands, stood and said: Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget? So he came out angry, dragging his garment, and asked, and was informed, and he prayed the rak'a he had omitted, then gave salam, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then gave salam."
"16587","468 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, (H). And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam in the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"16588","469 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Tawwab al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer and erred in his prayer, and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recited tashahhud, then gave salam."
"16589","470 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulaya narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr as three rak'as, then entered, and a man called al-Khirbaq stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, mentioning to him what he had done. So he came out angry, dragging his cloak, until he reached the people, and said: Is this one truthful? They said: Yes. So he prayed that rak'a, then gave salam, then prostrated two prostrations, then gave salam."
"16590","Chapter. 471 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-A'la informed us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lost, and a woman intended to slaughter it, and they told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I had vowed to slaughter it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one has a vow regarding what he does not own."
"16591","Chapter. 472 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that when the death of al-Najashi reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. So he stood and prayed over him with the people behind him."
"16592","Yunus ibn Ubayd from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Muhallab from Imran. 473 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. So he stood and we prayed behind him, and I was in the second row, and he prayed over him."
"16593","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Muhallab from Imran ibn Husayn. 474 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman from Juhayna confessed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to adultery, and said: I am pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she delivers, inform me. He did so, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding her, and her clothes were fastened around her, then he ordered her stoning, and she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you stone her, then pray over her? He said: She has repented a repentance which, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madina, it would have encompassed them. And have you found better than that she gave her life for Allah the Exalted?"
"16594","475 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdillah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdillah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, Abu al-Muhallab narrated to me, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her guardian: Take good care of her, and when she delivers what is in her womb, bring her to me. When she delivered, he brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and her clothes were tightened upon her, and he ordered regarding her, and she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you stoned her, then prayed over her? He said: She has repented a repentance which, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madina, it would have encompassed them. And have you found better than that she gave her life for Allah the Exalted?"
"16595","476 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim and Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from his uncle, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16596","477 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr and Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while pregnant from adultery, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin, so establish it upon me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she delivers what is in her womb, bring her to me. He did so, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding her, and her clothes were fastened upon her, then he ordered regarding her, and she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Do you pray over her though she committed adultery? He said: She has repented a repentance which, had it been divided among ninety of the people of Madina, it would have encompassed them. Have you found better than that she gave her life for Allah the Exalted?"
"16597","478 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, Abu al-Muhallab narrated to me, that Imran ibn Husayn narrated to him, that a woman from Juhayna committed adultery and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), being pregnant from adultery, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she delivers what is in her womb, bring her to me. He did so, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and her clothes were held upon her, then he ordered regarding her, and she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar said to him: Do you pray over her though she committed adultery? He said: She has repented a repentance which, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madina, it would have encompassed them. And have you found better than that she gave her life for Allah the Exalted?"
"16598","479 - Musa ibn Harun and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Hudba ibn Khalid informed us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, that Abu Qilaba narrated to him, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me, while she was pregnant. He ordered her guardian to treat her well until she delivered, and when she delivered, he ordered her clothes, and they were fastened upon her, then he stoned her, and prayed over her. Umar said: O Prophet of Allah, do you pray over her though she committed adultery? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, she has repented a repentance which, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madina, it would have encompassed them. And have you found better than that she gave her life for Allah the Exalted?"
"16599","480 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard a woman curse a she-camel, and he said: Take your goods, for it has become binding upon it. Imran said: It is as if I look at it, a grey she-camel."
"16600","481 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a woman was on a she-camel, and it cried out and she cursed it, he said: Take your goods off it, for it has become binding upon it."
"16601","482 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him."
"16602","483 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that Abu Musa came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts, and he mentioned the hadith."
"16603","Imran ibn Hudayr from Abu Qilaba. 484 - Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Raja'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Ma'dani narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah al-Misma'i narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman was on a she-camel, and it cried out and she cursed it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw off its goods from it, for it is cursed."
"16604","al-Zubayr Abu Muhammad al-Hanzali from Imran. 485 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from his father, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16605","486 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayda narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16606","487 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad al-Hanzali, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is an oath."
"16607","488 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16608","489 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, from Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id, Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, my father informed me, that a man narrated to him that he asked Imran ibn Husayn about a man who vowed not to attend prayer in the mosque of his people, and Imran said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"16609","490 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from a man from the people of Basra, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is an oath."
"16610","Hafs al-Laythi from Imran ibn Husayn. 491 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (H). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Hafs al-Laythi, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam jars, wearing silk, and wearing gold rings."
"16611","492 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Hafs al-Laythi, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam jars."
"16612","Hujayr ibn al-Rabi' from Imran ibn Husayn. 493 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Abu Na'ama Amr ibn Isa al-Adawi narrated to us, Hujayr ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Ka'b said: Part of it is weakness. Imran said: O Hujayr, who is this? I said: This is a man from us in whom there is no harm. He said: He hears me narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and says part of it is weakness and part of it dignity for Allah; by Allah, I will not narrate to you a hadith today."
"16613","al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj from Imran ibn al-Husayn. 494 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar informed us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seventy thousand of my umma will enter Paradise without reckoning, those who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqya, nor take evil omens, and upon their Lord they rely. Calamity kept befalling us until we cauterized, but we did not prosper nor succeed."
"16614","495 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawra al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, he said: Imran ibn Husayn said: I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16615","Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini from Imran ibn Husayn. 496 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhra, from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Some people from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Accept the glad tidings, O Banu Tamim. They said: You have given us glad tidings, so give us. That was seen on his face. Then some people from the people of Yemen came, and he said: Accept the glad tidings, since Banu Tamim did not accept them. They said: We have accepted, O Messenger of Allah."
"16616","497 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted existed and nothing else existed, and His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Reminder everything that will be, then He created the heavens. And a speaker said: Overtake your she-camel. So I stood, and the mirage was breaking short of it; would that it had gone and I had fully heard the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16617","498 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhra, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a she-camel, and I tied it at the door, then entered, and some people from Banu Tamim came to him, and he said: Accept the glad tidings. They said: We have accepted, so give us. So he turned away from them. Then some people from Yemen came to him, and he said: Accept the glad tidings, and do not say as Banu Tamim said. They said: We have accepted, so tell us about the beginning of this matter. He said: Allah existed and nothing else existed, and His Throne was upon the water. Then a man came and said: O Ibn Husayn, overtake your she-camel. So I went and caught up with it at the mirage; by Allah, I wished I had left it."
"16618","499 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same, with the addition: And He created the Reminder. Abu al-Qasim said: This wording Muhammad ibn Ubayd used to err in, and Ahmad ibn Hanbal would forbid him from narrating it; the correct version is what Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and others narrated: And He wrote the Reminder."
"16619","500 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq al-Fazari, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I tied my she-camel at the door, then entered, and some people from Banu Tamim came to him, and he said: Accept the glad tidings, O Banu Tamim. They said: You have given us glad tidings, so give us. Then some people from the people of Yemen came to him, and he said: Accept the glad tidings, O people of Yemen, since Banu Tamim did not accept them. They said: That we may learn the religion, and ask you about the beginning of this matter, how was it? He said: Allah the Exalted existed and nothing else existed, and His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Reminder everything, then He created the heavens and the earth. Then a man came to me and said: Overtake your she-camel, for it has gone. So I went out and found it with the mirage breaking short of it; by Allah, I wished I had left it."
"16620","Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, whose name is Hassan ibn Hurayth, from Imran ibn Husayn. 501 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalid ibn Rabah informed us, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"16621","502 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, both said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Rabah, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"16622","503 - Ahmad ibn Rushd ibn al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ashhal ibn Hatim, from Qurra ibn Khalid, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Modesty is all good."
"16623","504 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu Na'ama narrated to us, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Ka'b said: Part of it is weakness and part of it dignity for Allah. Imran said to Bushayr: You hear me narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say: Part of it is weakness and part of it dignity. And he became angry and said: I will not narrate to you a hadith today."
"16624","505 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Modesty brings nothing but good."
"16625","506 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty brings nothing but good."
"16626","507 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa' narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a young girl in her chamber, and when he disliked something, it was known on his face."
"16627","508 - al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Sulayman ibn Umayr ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Murra narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something, that was known on his face."
"16628","509 - Abd al-A'li ibn Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Fadl al-Humaydi and Raja' al-Bazzar narrated to us, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"16629","Abu Hassan al-A'raj, whose name is Muslim, from Imran ibn Husayn. 510 - Abdillah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, (H). And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would narrate to us at night about Banu Isra'il, and we would not stand except for the major prayer."
"16630","Abu Mijlaz Lahiq ibn Humayd from Imran ibn Husayn. 511 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim narrated to us, both said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, but we cauterized, and there is in it neither cure for illness nor absolution from sin."
"16631","Abu Nadra al-Mundhir ibn Malik al-Abdi from Imran ibn Husayn. 512 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, (H). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, that Mu'adh ibn Hisham, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu Nadra, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a boy belonging to poor people cut the ear of a boy belonging to rich people, and his family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are poor. So he imposed nothing upon them."
"16632","513 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Nadra, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never traveled except that he prayed two rak'as until he returned, and he stayed in Makka twelve days, praying two rak'as, then saying: O people of Makka, stand and pray two rak'as, for we are travelers. And he raided al-Ta'if and Hunayn and prayed two rak'as, then came to al-Ji'irrana and performed Umra from it."
"16633","514 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Nadra, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16634","515 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulaya narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadra, he said: Imran ibn al-Husayn passed by our gathering, and a young man from the people stood up to him and asked him about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in raids, Hajj, and Umra. So he came and stood over us and said: This one asked me about a matter, and I wanted you to hear it. I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed only two rak'as until he returned to Madina. And I witnessed the Conquest with him; he stayed in Makka eighteen nights, praying only two rak'as. And I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and raided, and he prayed only two rak'as until he returned to Madina. And I performed Hajj with Uthman for seven years of his rule, and he prayed only two rak'as, then he prayed four at Mina."
"16635","516 - Abdillah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Warith, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadra, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed only two rak'as until he returned to Madina. And I performed Hajj with him, and he prayed only two rak'as until he returned, and he stayed in Makka eighteen nights, praying two rak'as and saying: Complete the prayer, O people of Makka, for we are travelers."
"16636","517 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yasin al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Nadra, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makka, he stayed there eighteen nights, leading the people of Makka in two rak'as except Maghrib, then saying: O people of Makka, complete your prayer, for we are travelers."
"16637","Uqba ibn Wassaj from Imran ibn al-Husayn. 518 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdillah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Kathir ibn Marwan al-Filastini narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla narrated to us, from Uqba ibn Wassaj, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for a man as evil is that he be pointed at with fingers."
"16638","Zurara ibn Awfa from Imran ibn al-Husayn. 519 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led his companions in Zuhr, and when he finished his prayer, he said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? Some of the people said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I knew that one of you contested it with me."
"16639","520 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, (H). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with his companions and said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: I did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew that a man contested it with me."
"16640","521 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (H). And Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16641","522 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers, either Zuhr or Asr. He said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: I did. He said: I knew that a man contested it with me."
"16642","523 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, (H). And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, and when he gave salam, he said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I knew that one of you contested it with me."
"16643","524 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Ala' informed us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, and when he turned, he said: Which of you contested the sura with me? A man said: I did, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended only good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I thought that a man contested it with me."
"16644","525 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulaya narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Zuhr prayer, and when he gave salam, he said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man from the people said so, and he said: I thought that one of you contested it with me."
"16645","526 - Darar ibn Sufyan al-Qattan al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."
"16646","527 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, (H). And Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ku'bari narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, (H). And Muhammad ibn Fada' al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, they said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my umma is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them - and Allah knows whether he mentioned the third or not - then there will arise people who testify though they are not asked to testify, and vow but do not fulfill, and betray and are not trusted, and obesity will spread among them."
"16647","528 - al-Hasan ibn Alluya al-Qattan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq and Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of this umma is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, three times, and Allah knows whether he mentioned the third or not. Then there will arise people who testify though they are not asked to testify, and vow but do not fulfill, and betray and are not trusted, and obesity will spread among them."
"16648","529 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, (H). And Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of this umma is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them. Then there will arise people who vow but do not fulfill, and swear though they are not asked to swear, and obesity will spread among them."
"16649","530 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, both said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, (H). And Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, both said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit another man's hand and knocked out his front tooth, and they disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: One of you bites his brother as the stallion bites; you have no blood-money."
"16650","531 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn: That a man bit another man's hand, and the biter's front tooth was pulled out, and he came to the Prophet and mentioned it to him, and he annulled that."
"16651","532 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit another on his forearm, and he pulled it away and his front tooth was pulled out, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he annulled it and said: Did you intend to bite your brother's flesh as the stallion bites?"
"16652","533 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit another man's hand, and he pulled his hand from his mouth, and his front tooth fell out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled it, or he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) voided it."
"16653","534 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Ayyub Abu al-Ala', from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit another man's hand, and he pulled his hand from him, and his two front teeth fell out, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he annulled it, then said: One of you eats his brother's flesh as the stallion eats, or as the stallion bites."
"16654","535 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Mujja'a ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit another man's forearm, and his front tooth was pulled out, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled it."
"16655","536 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"16656","537 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High."
"16657","538 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, (H). And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha' Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, both from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"16658","539 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqba al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My umma is pardoned for what their souls speak of, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it."
"16659","540 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Adam al-Basri narrated to us, at al-Missisa, al-Mu'alla ibn Baraka narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my umma in its early mornings. When he wanted to dispatch an expedition, he sent it out early."
"16660","Hayyaj ibn Imran from Imran ibn Husayn. 541 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj, that a slave boy of his father fled, and he made a vow that if he got hold of him, he would cut off a piece of him. When he got hold of him, he sent me to Imran ibn al-Husayn, and I asked him, and Imran said: Order your father to free his slave or expiate for his oath, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge us to charity and forbid us mutilation. So I went to Samura and asked him, and he said the same as Imran said. Thus Ma'mar and Hammam and Qatada narrated it, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj; and Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba and Hammam ibn Yahya differed from him."
"16661","542 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, that Hayyaj ibn Imran came to Imran ibn Husayn, and his father had said regarding a slave boy of his who fled: If he got hold of him, he would cut off a piece of him, or his hand. He got hold of him, and Hayyaj went to Imran and asked him about that, and told him his father's words. Imran said: Order your father to expiate his oath, or free his slave, and not cut off a piece of him, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his sermon used to urge charity and forbid mutilation. Then he reported that he went to Samura ibn Jundub, and he said the same as Imran said."
"16662","543 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj ibn Imran al-Burjumi, that a slave boy of his father fled, and he made it a vow to Allah the Exalted that if he got hold of him, he would cut off his hand. When he came to him, meaning to Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Tell your father: Let him not do it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urge charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation. Tell your father: Let him expiate for his oath and pardon his slave."
"16663","al-Hilal ibn Ziyad al-Adawi from Imran ibn Husayn. 544 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatada, from al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man divorced but did not call witnesses, and took her back but did not call witnesses, and he said: He divorced outside the waiting period and took her back outside the Sunna; let him call witnesses to his divorce and to his return."
"16664","545 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Mujja'a ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A man said to him: I divorced my wife openly and took her back secretly? Imran said: You divorced outside the waiting period and took her back outside the Sunna; fear Allah and call witnesses."
"16665","546 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We were with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his voice with these two verses: O mankind, fear your Lord; indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a great thing. On the Day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nursed. When we heard that, we urged the mounts, and we knew he was about to say something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say. When they gathered around him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know which day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is the day Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: Adam, stand and send forth the delegation of the Fire. He will say: O Lord, and how many is the delegation of the Fire? He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety. When they heard that, they despaired until they did not show a laughing tooth. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what was with them, he laughed and said: Act and receive glad tidings; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, with you are two creations who were never with anyone but they made them numerous. They said: Who, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and those who perished from the children of Adam and Iblis. Then he said: Act and receive glad tidings; by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you among people are but like the mole on the side of a camel, or the mark on the foreleg of an animal."
"16666","Habib ibn Abi Fadala from Imran ibn Husayn. 547 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Surad ibn Abi al-Manazil narrated to us, he said: I heard Habib ibn Abi Fadala al-Makki, he said: When this mosque, the congregational mosque, was built, he said, with Imran ibn Husayn sitting, and they mentioned intercession in his presence, and a man from the people said: O Abu Nujayd, you narrate to us hadiths for which we find no basis in the Qur'an. Imran ibn Husayn became angry and said to a man: Have you read the Qur'an? He said: Yes. He said: Did you find in it Maghrib prayer as three, Isha prayer as four, morning prayer as two, the first as four, and Asr as four? He said: No. He said: From whom did you take this matter? Did you not take it from us, and we took it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Did you find: In every forty dirhams a dirham, and in every so many sheep so much, and in every so many camels so much; did you find that in the Qur'an? He said: No. He said: From whom did you take this? We took it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and you took it from us. He said: Did you find in the Qur'an: And let them circumambulate the Ancient House? Did you find: Circumambulate seven times, and pray two rak'as behind the Maqam; did you find this in the Qur'an? From whom did you take it? Did you not take it from us, and we took it from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Did you find in the Qur'an: No jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam? He said: No. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam. Did you hear Allah say to peoples in His Book: What put you into Saqar? They will say: We were not of those who prayed, nor did we feed the poor, until he reached: So the intercession of intercessors will not benefit them. Habib said: I heard him say: Intercession."
"16667","al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hashimi from Imran. 548 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (H). And Shu'ayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: Abu Husayn ibn Ubayd came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What do you think of a man who honors the guest and maintains kinship ties, and does this and that? He is your father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think of my father and your father, for they are in the Fire? He did not remain after that but twenty nights until he died."
"16668","549 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hashimi, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that his father Husayn came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think of a man who used to honor the guest and maintain kinship ties, who died before you, and he is your father? He said: My father and your father and you are in the Fire. Husayn died a polytheist."
"16669","Abu al-Dahma' from Imran ibn Husayn. 550 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, both said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahma', from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears of al-Dajjal, let him stay away from him. By Allah, a man will come to him thinking he is a believer, then follow him because of what he sees of doubts."
"16670","551 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Dahma', from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you hears of al-Dajjal, let him flee from him, for a man will come to him thinking he is a believer, then follow him because of what he sees of doubts."
"16671","552 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, (H). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, both from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Dahma', from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears of al-Dajjal, let him stay away from him - (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - for a man will come to him thinking he is a believer, then seeing what is with him of doubts, he will follow him."
"16672","Abu Qatada, whose name is Tamim ibn Nudayr, from Imran. 553 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu al-Nu'man Arim narrated to us, (H). And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (H). And Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd, from Abu Qatada, he said: We entered upon Imran ibn Husayn, with us Bushayr ibn Ka'b, and Imran said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Ka'b said: O Abu Nujayd, we find in some books that part of it is tranquility and dignity, and part of it is weakness. Imran repeated the hadith, and Bushayr repeated his words to him, and Imran became angry until his cheeks reddened. He said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you oppose me with books. So we said: O Abu Nujayd, he is a man from the people of the house."
"16673","554 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatada, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Modesty is all good."
"16674","Abd al-Malik ibn Ya'la the judge from Imran ibn Husayn. 555 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Allaf narrated to us, Bashir ibn Surayj al-Bazzar narrated to us, from Qabisa ibn al-Ja'd al-Sulami, from Abu al-Malih, from Abd al-Malik ibn Ya'la, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who sells old inherited property but Allah the Exalted sets upon him something destructive."
"16675","Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali from Imran ibn Husayn. 556 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Uqaysh ibn Rabas al-Asadi narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali: That he asked Imran ibn Husayn, Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b about qadar, and said: I disputed with the people of qadar until they distressed me, so do you have knowledge to narrate to me? They said: Had Allah the Exalted punished the people of heaven and earth, He would have punished them without wronging them, and had He admitted them into His mercy, His mercy would have been wider than their sins; but as He decreed, He punishes whom He wills and has mercy on whom He wills. Whoever is punished, that is the truth, and whoever is shown mercy, that is the truth. Had you like Uhud to spend in the path of Allah, it would not be accepted from you until you believe in all of qadar, its good and its evil. Then Imran said to Abu al-Aswad when he narrated the hadith to him: I heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abdillah and Ubayy ibn Ka'b heard it with me. Abu al-Aswad asked them both, and they narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16676","557 - Narrated to us Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar, narrated to us 'Uthman ibn 'Umar, narrated to us 'Azrah ibn Thabit, (h). And narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani, narrated to us 'Awn ibn 'Umarah, narrated to us 'Azrah ibn Thabit, from Yahya ibn 'Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do you see what people do today and strive in - is it something decreed upon them, or past upon them from a preordained decree that preceded, or in what they will face of what their Prophet brought them and the proof was established upon them thereby? He said: Rather it is something decreed upon them and past upon them. He said: Then why do they act? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah created for one of the two abodes, He enables him for its deed - the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah: {By the soul and He Who proportioned it, then inspired it its wickedness and its piety}."
"16677","Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Du'ali, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 558 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi, narrated to us Abu Zuhayr 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra', he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Faddalah said: We were discussing righteousness with Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad. Abu Harb said: We were discussing righteousness with 'Imran ibn Husayn, and 'Imran ibn Husayn said: We were discussing righteousness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began narrating to us, saying: Among the nations before you there was a worshipful man of a hermitage called Jurayj. He had a mother who would come to him and call him, and he would look down to her and speak to her. One day she came to him while he was in his prayer occupied with it, and she called him - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imitated her, placing his hand on his forehead - and she kept calling him, raising her head, placing her hand on her forehead: O Jurayj, O Jurayj, three times, each time three times; each time Jurayj said: O my Lord, my mother or my prayer? So she became angry and said: O Allah, let Jurayj not die until he looks into the faces of prostitutes. He said: And the daughter of the king of the town had matured, and she became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said to her: Who did this to you? Who is your companion? She said: He is the man of the hermitage, Jurayj. He was unaware until he heard axes at the base of his hermitage. He kept asking them: Woe to you, what is wrong with you? They did not answer him. When he saw that, he took a rope and let himself down, and they began dragging him by his nose and beating him, saying: A show-off who deceives people with his deeds. He said to them: Woe to you, what is wrong with you? They said: Are you the companion of the king's daughter whom you made pregnant? He said: Then what did she do? They said: She gave birth to a boy. He said: Is the boy alive? They said: Yes. He said: Step away from me. So they stepped away, and he prayed two rak'ahs, then finished, then walked to a tree and took a branch from it, then the boy was brought while in his cradle, and he struck him with that branch and said: O tyrant, who is your father? He said: My father is so-and-so the shepherd. They said: If you wish we will build your hermitage for you with gold, and if you wish with silver. He said: Return it as it was. Abu Harb claimed that none spoke in the cradle except three: 'Isa son of Maryam, the witness of Yusuf, and the companion of Jurayj."
"16678","'Ata, the freedman of 'Imran ibn Husayn, from 'Imran. 559 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Ata, the freedman of 'Imran ibn Husayn, from his father, that 'Imran ibn Husayn was appointed over the charity, and he went and then returned, and they said to him: Where is the wealth? He said: Did you send me for wealth? We took it as we used to take it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we placed it as we used to place it."
"16679","Abu Qilabah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 560 - Narrated to us Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti, narrated to us Safwan ibn Salih, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Nasri, that he heard al-Mutawakkil ibn al-Layth narrating from Abu Qilabah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, and Samurah ibn Jundub, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white, and shroud your dead in it."
"16680","561 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Waki', from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn: that a man freed six slaves at his death, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded regarding him, and freed two and kept four in slavery."
"16681","Al-Sumayt ibn Sumayr, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 562 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sumayt ibn Sumayr, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and a man charged against a man of the polytheists. When he overcame him with the spear, he said: I am a Muslim. So he killed him, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have sinned, so seek forgiveness for me. He said: And what is that? He said: I charged against a man of the polytheists, and when I overcame him with the spear he said: I am a Muslim, but I thought he was seeking refuge, so I killed him. He said: Why did you not split open his heart until it became clear to you? He said: And would it become clear to me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He spoke to you with his tongue, yet you did not believe him for what he said in his heart. He said: Then the man died and we buried him, and he came to be upon the surface of the earth. So we ordered our youths and they guarded him, and he came to be upon the surface of the earth. We said: They were heedless, so we guarded him, and he came to be upon the surface of the earth. So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Indeed it accepts one worse than him, but Allah wanted to teach you the sanctity of blood. Then he said: Take him to the foot of this mountain and pile stones over him. So we did."
"16682","Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 563 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Harish, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti, narrated to us Ziyad al-Jassas, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: When 'Ali prevailed over the people of Basra, he led them in prayer like the prayer of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the takbir when he bowed, when he raised his head, when he prostrated, and when he stood from the two rak'ahs."
"16683","564 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad and Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri, they said: Narrated to us Salamah ibn Shabib, narrated to us Husayn al-Ju'fi, narrated to us Za'idah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Khalid ibn Ayyub, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him keep away from him."
"16684","565 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Zuhayr, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Dinar, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, or Humayd ibn Hilal, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, or 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty, all of it, is good."
"16685","566 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Zuhayr, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Dinar, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, or Humayd ibn Hilal, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, or 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of pellet-shooting, for it breaks the tooth and gouges the eye, and does not harm the enemy."
"16686","'Uqbah ibn Wassaj, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 567 - Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us Kathir ibn Marwan, from Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Ablah, from 'Uqbah ibn Wassaj, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient sin for a man that fingers be pointed at him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he is good? He said: Even if he is good, it is evil for him except whom Allah has mercy upon; and if he is evil, then it is evil."
"16687","Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 568 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Shabab al-'Usfuri, narrated to us Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn Khalid narrating from 'Abd Allah ibn Ghalib, from Abu al-Malih, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire."
"16688","569 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya, he said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Humayd narrating from Abu al-Malih, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, she committed adultery - she said that repeatedly. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you will shelter this woman? A man of the people said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Go with her, let her wait, and when she delivers, bring her to me. So he brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after she delivered, and he ordered concerning her and she was stoned. Then he said to his Companions: Step forward and pray over her. 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, do you pray over her? He said: She has repented a repentance, if seventy of the people of Madinah repented it, it would be accepted from them."
"16689","Abu Murayah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 570 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, concerning Abu Murayah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah."
"16690","571 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Abu Murayah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to Allah."
"16691","Bajalah ibn 'Abdah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 572 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ma'in, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, he said: I heard Abu Nasr al-Hilali narrating from Bajalah ibn 'Abdah - or 'Abdah ibn Bajalah, he said: I said to 'Imran ibn Husayn: Inform me of the most hated people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Keep it secret from me until I die? I said: Yes. He said: The most hated people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Banu Hanifah, Banu Umayyah, and Thaqif."
"16692","'Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-'Uqayli, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 573 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, narrated to us Jarir, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-'Uqayli, he said: I was walking with 'Imran ibn Husayn and we reached the mosque of Basra, and Buraydah was sitting, and Sukbah, a man of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Aslam, was standing praying Duha. Buraydah said: O 'Imran, can you not pray as Sukbah prays? He said that only as if he meant him by it. He said: So 'Imran fell silent and we went on. 'Imran said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we faced Uhud and climbed it, and he looked over Madinah and said: Woe to its mother, a town whose people will leave it in its best state; the Dajjal will come to it but will not be able to enter it - he will find upon each of its passes an angel with sword unsheathed. Then we came down and came to the mosque, and a man was praying, and he said: Who is this? I said: So-and-so, and of his affair - and I began praising him. He said: Do not let him hear, lest you break his back. Then he raised my hands and said: The best of your religion is its easiest. Abu al-Qasim said: Thus al-A'mash narrated it, from Abu Bishr, from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from 'Imran ibn Husayn; and Shu'bah and Abu 'Awanah differed from him, narrating it from Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Raja' ibn Abi Raja', from Mihjan ibn al-Adra'."
"16693","Bajalah al-Qushayri, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 574 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khayyat al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami, narrated to us al-Fadl ibn 'Abd Allah al-Sari, from al-Rabi' ibn Badr, from Rashid ibn Nujayh al-Himmani, from Junadah, from Bajalah al-Qushayri, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while hating these three Arab tribes: Thaqif, Banu Umayyah, and Banu Hanifah."
"16694","575 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from his father, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Bajalah ibn 'Abdah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while hating three tribes: Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."
"16695","576 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat, both sons of Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far al-Razi, from his father, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub, from 'Abdah ibn Bajalah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16696","Abu Tulayhah, freedman of Banu Khalaf, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 577 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Fasawi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Harawi, narrated to us al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari, from Hisham ibn Ziyad, he said: Narrated to me my brother al-Walid ibn Ziyad, from Abu Tulayhah, freedman of Banu Khalaf, narrated to us 'Imran ibn Husayn, that he witnessed 'Uthman ibn 'Affan in the days of the Tabuk expedition, in the army of hardship. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered charity, strength and mutual support. The Arab Christians had written to Heraclius: This man who has come forth claiming prophethood has perished, and years of drought have struck them so their wealth has perished; if you wish to rejoin your religion, now is the time. So he sent a man of their notables called al-Danad, and equipped with him forty thousand. When that reached the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he wrote among the Arabs, and he would sit the whole day upon the pulpit supplicating Allah, saying: O Allah, if this band perishes, You will not be worshipped on earth. The people had no strength, and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan had equipped a caravan to Syria intending to bring provisions upon it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, these are two hundred camels with their saddles and blankets, and two hundred ounces. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah, and the people magnified Allah. Then he stood in another standing and ordered charity, so 'Uthman stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, and these are another two hundred and two hundred ounces. So he magnified Allah and the people magnified. 'Uthman brought the camels and brought the wealth, and poured it before him, and I heard him saying: Nothing 'Uthman does after today will harm him."
"16697","'Imran ibn 'Isam, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 578 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Khalid ibn Qays and Hammam, they said: Narrated to us Qatadah, from 'Imran ibn 'Isam, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the even and the odd, and he said: It is the prayer; of it is even and of it is odd."
"16698","579 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge, they said: Narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from 'Imran ibn 'Isam, from a man of the people of Basra, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the even and the odd: It is the prayer; of it is even, and of it is odd."
"16699","Zahdam al-Jarmi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 580 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, (h). And narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, they said: Narrated to us Aban ibn Yazid al-'Attar, narrated to us Abu Jamrah, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my ummah is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will arise peoples who testify though they are not asked to testify, and swear though they are not asked to swear, and betray though they are not trusted, and obesity will spread among them."
"16700","581 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abdaws ibn Kamil, narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, (h). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Hakam, they said: Narrated to us Shu'bah, from Abu Jamrah, narrated to me Zahdam ibn Mudarrib, he said: I heard 'Imran ibn al-Husayn saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. 'Imran said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned after his generation two generations or three. Then there will be after them a people who testify though they are not asked to testify, and betray though they are not trusted, and speak yet do not fulfill, and obesity will appear among them. And the wording is that of 'Amr ibn Hakam."
"16701","582 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Abu Jamrah, from Zahdam, from 'Imran, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16702","Narration of the Kufans: Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 583 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani, narrated to us Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from al-A'mash, from 'Ali ibn Mudrik, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my ummah is the generation among whom I am, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who grow fat and love fatness, and give testimony without being asked for it."
"16703","584 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Shayban, from al-A'mash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, he said: I was in Basra and entered the mosque, and there was an old man with people gathered over him narrating to them, and I heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come after them a people who grow fat and love fatness, giving testimony before they are asked for it. I said: Who is this? They said: 'Imran ibn al-Husayn."
"16704","585 - Narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us Sahl ibn 'Uthman, (h). And narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: Narrated to us Waki', from al-A'mash, narrated to us Hilal ibn Yasaf al-Ashja'i, he said: I heard 'Imran ibn Husayn saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who grow fat and love fatness, giving testimony before they are asked for it."
"16705","586 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd, from al-A'mash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Imran ibn al-Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16706","'Amir al-Sha'bi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 587 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Idris and Ibn Fudayl, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he raised it, he said: There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a venomous sting."
"16707","588 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Malik ibn Mighwal, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a venomous sting."
"16708","'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 589 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he was a man with piles - about the prayer of a man standing and sitting. He said: His prayer sitting is half of his prayer standing."
"16709","590 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abu Usamah, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one lying is half of the prayer of one sitting."
"16710","591 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri, narrated to us 'Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki, narrated to us 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id, narrated to us Husayn al-Mu'allim, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he was a man with piles - about the prayer of one sitting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one lying is half of the prayer of one sitting."
"16711","592 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of a man sitting. He said: His prayer standing is better; and his prayer sitting is half of his prayer standing, and his prayer lying is half of his prayer sitting."
"16712","593 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, they said: Narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Husayn al-Mu'allim, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What I fear most for you after me is every eloquent-tongued hypocrite."
"16713","Rib'i ibn Hirash, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 594 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us 'Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sulami, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i ibn Hirash - Muhammad said: Had I said that I heard it from Rib'i I would have spoken truly - from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. So he gave it to 'Ali."
"16714","595 - Narrated to us Abu Ma'n Thabit ibn Nu'aym al-Hawji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-'Asqalani, narrated to us Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, from his father, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. So he gave it to 'Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
"16715","596 - Narrated to us Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Salih al-Aswad, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. Then he called 'Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and gave it to him."
"16716","597 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini, narrated to us Kathir ibn Yahya, narrated to us Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Karim ibn Salit ibn 'Atiyyah al-Hanafi, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. So he called 'Ali and gave it to him."
"16717","598 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas al-Razi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Humayd, narrated to us Harun ibn al-Mughirah, from 'Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from 'Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. So he gave it to 'Ali."
"16718","599 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Raja', informed us Shayban, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, or from a man, that Husayn came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, 'Abd al-Muttalib was better to his people than you; he used to feed them liver and hump, while you slaughter them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him what Allah willed him to say. He said: What do you command me to say? He said: Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul, and decree for me the soundest of my affair."
"16719","Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 600 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abdaws ibn Kamil, narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, narrated to us Abu al-Mughirah, meaning al-Nadr ibn Isma'il al-Bajali, from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali, (h). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Ma'qil ibn Malik, (h). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Ibn 'A'ishah and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr ibn Muslim ibn al-Rabi' ibn Muslim, they said: Narrated to us al-Nadr ibn Isma'il, from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Fatimah, stand and witness your sacrifice, for you will be forgiven with the first drop of its blood for every sin you committed; and say: {Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, no partner has He; and with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims}. 'Imran said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for you and the people of your house specially - for you are worthy of that - or for the Muslims generally? He said: Rather for the Muslims generally."
"16720","Nufay' ibn al-Harith Abu Dawud, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 601 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Ubaydah, narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Nu'man al-Bahili, narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Hazawwar, from Nufay', from 'Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Barzah, that they said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a funeral, and he saw people who had cast off their cloaks walking in undershirts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you adopt the practice of Jahiliyyah? I had intended to supplicate against you a supplication by which you would return in other than your forms. So they took their cloaks and did not return to that."
"16721","602 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Nufay' ibn al-Harith, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no judge among the judges of the Muslims but with him are two angels guiding him to the truth so long as he does not intend other than it; when he intends other than it and deliberately deviates, the two angels disown him and leave him to himself."
"16722","603 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, from al-A'mash, from Abu Dawud, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man has a right due from a man and he defers it to its term, it is charity for him; and if he defers it after its term, he has charity for each day."
"16723","Bilal ibn Yahya al-'Absi, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 604 - Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Zakariyya, from Sa'd al-'Absi, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I fear for Quraysh only from themselves. I said: And what is it? He said: Covetous, grasping ones; if your life is prolonged you will see them the most covetous, grasping of people, until you see people among them like sheep between two watering troughs, once to this and once to this."
"16724","'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 605 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Hisab al-Raqqi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi, narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: The prophets were presented to me; a prophet would come with none but one man with him, and a prophet would come with none but two men with him, and a prophet would come with none but a small group likewise. Then I looked and saw a great multitude, and I thought they were my ummah; when they drew near, they were the people of Musa. Then it was said to me: Look. So I looked and said: Who are these? He said: It was said: These are your ummah. So I rejoiced at that and was gladdened. Then it was said: Look. So I looked, and there was also a great multitude. It was said: These are your ummah. So I rejoiced and was gladdened. It was said to me: With these are seventy thousand of your ummah who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and the Muslims said: Who are these seventy thousand? Their opinion agreed that it is one born in Islam who never encountered anything of polytheism. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while we were upon that, and said: They are those who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqyah, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. 'Ukkashah stood and said: Supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: O Allah, make him of them. Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: 'Ukkashah has preceded you to it."
"16725","Raja' ibn Haywah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 606 - Narrated to us Abu 'Awanah Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hafs, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Matar al-Warraq, from Raja' ibn Haywah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bringing animals from afar and taking them afar for racing deception, and forbade touching and najsh along with sale, and forbade that a man sell over the sale of his brother, or propose over the proposal of his brother."
"16726","Al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from 'Imran. 607 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi, from Musa ibn 'Ubaydah, from al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Mighty and Majestic loves His servant, the believing, poor, abstinent father of children."
"16727","608 - Narrated to us Abu 'Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Kufi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, from Musa ibn 'Ubaydah, from al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from 'Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Mighty and Majestic loves the chaste, abstinent father of children."
"16728","Unnamed men, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. 609 - Narrated to us Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani, narrated to us Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, from his father, narrated to me al-Sumayt, from Abu al-'Ala', narrated to me a youth of the tribe, that 'Imran ibn al-Husayn narrated to him, that 'Abs or Ibn 'Abs among people of Khath'am came to him. 'Imran said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Raid Banu so-and-so with so-and-so. He said: So we lined up the men, and the women were behind the men. Then when they returned, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, may Allah forgive you. He said: Have you done something new? He said: When the people were routed, I caught up with a man of the people and the women, and he said: I am a Muslim - or he said: I have become Muslim - so I killed him. No, by Allah, I did not do it. So he did not seek forgiveness for him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what do I fight people except for Islam? By Allah, I shall not seek forgiveness for you - or as he said. He said: Then he died afterwards, and his clan buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out. Then they buried him and guarded him a second time, and the earth cast him out. Then they said: Perhaps someone came while you were asleep and took him out. So they buried him a third time and guarded him, and the earth cast him out a third time. When they saw that, they cast him aside - or as he said."
"16729","'Imran Abu Abi Jamrah, he has Companionship. 610 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Affan ibn Muslim and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, they said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Jamrah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three years old."
"16730","'Imran ibn Taym Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi, a mukhadram. 611 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi is 'Imran ibn 'Abd Allah."
"16731","612 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in saying: Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi died in the year one hundred and five."
"16732","613 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us 'Umarah al-Maghuli, he said: I heard Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent while I was a five-year-old, calling to Paradise."
"16733","614 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Hashraj ibn Nubatah, narrated to us Abu Nusayrah, narrated to us Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he entered a garden of one of the Ansar, and he was drawing water in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What will you give me if I water this garden of yours? He said: I strive to water it but cannot manage that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you give me one hundred dates that I choose from your dates? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the bucket and soon watered it until the man said: You have flooded my garden. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose from his dates one hundred dates, and he and his Companions ate until they were full, then he returned to him one hundred dates as he had taken from him."
"16734","'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami, kunya Abu Najih. 615 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Marzuq, informed us Shu'bah, from Abu al-Fayd, he said: I witnessed Mu'awiyah giving al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad a donkey. So a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah stood and said: What is it to you to take it? And what is it to Mu'awiyah to give you? As if I see you on the Day of Resurrection carrying it upon your neck, its head at its bottom."
"16735","616 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, informed us Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr, he said: And narrated to me Wahb, from Sa'id ibn Miqlas, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah - and he was a great old man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he loved to be taken to Him; he would supplicate: O Allah, my age has grown great and my bone has weakened, so take me to You. He said: While I was one day in the mosque of Damascus, a handsome young man of the most beautiful men, wearing a green cloak, said: What is this that you supplicate with? I said: How should I supplicate, O son of my brother? He said: Say: O Allah, make the deed good and let the term reach. I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Ribayil who draws grief from the hearts of the believers."
"16736","What al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah narrated: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 617 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished us with an admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled. We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so counsel us. He said: I counsel you with fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave; for whoever lives after me will see much disagreement. So hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, guided caliphs after me, and bite upon it with the molars; and beware of newly-invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance."
"16737","618 - Narrated to us Musa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi, narrated to us Haywah ibn Shurayh, (h). And narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished them one day with an admonition after the dawn prayer, from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us? He said: I counsel you with fear of Allah and hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave; for whoever of you lives after me will see much disagreement. So beware of newly-invented matters, for it is misguidance; and hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided caliphs after me - bite upon it with the molars."
"16738","619 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis,i narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, (h). And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, they said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Damrah ibn Habib, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Sulami, that he heard 'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished us with an admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled. We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us? He said: I have left you upon the clear white path, its night like its day; none deviates from it after me except one doomed. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement, so hold to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided caliphs; and hold to obedience even if it be an Abyssinian slave - bite upon it with the molars. For the believer is like the docile camel: wherever it is led, it follows."
"16739","620 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' al-Himsi, narrated to me my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, they said: Narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the dawn prayer, then mentioned the like of it."
"16740","621 - Narrated to us Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, narrated to me my father, narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, narrated to us Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from his uncle, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah - and 'Irbad was a man of Banu Sulaym - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and admonished the people, gave them hope and warned them, and said what Allah willed to be, and said: Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, and obey whomsoever Allah has placed over your affair, and do not dispute the command with its people even if he be a black slave. Hold to what you know of the Sunnah of your Prophet and the rightly-guided, guided caliphs, and bite upon it with the molars."
"16741","Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta', from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 622 - Narrated to us Abu 'Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala' ibn Zabr, narrated to me my father, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta', from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one morning and admonished us with an admonition from which hearts trembled and eyes shed tears. We said: O Messenger of Allah, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so enjoin upon us. He said: Hold to fear of Allah and hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave; those who remain after me will see severe disagreement. So hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided caliphs, and bite upon it with the molars; and beware of newly-invented matters, for every newly-invented matter is misguidance."
"16742","Al-Muhasir ibn Habib, from al-'Irbad. 623 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir, from Muhasir ibn Habib, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished us after the dawn prayer with an eloquent admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled. A man of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell. He said: I counsel you with fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave; for whoever of you lives will see much disagreement. So beware of newly-invented matters, for it is innovation; whoever of you reaches that, let him hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, guided caliphs - bite upon it with the molars."
"16743","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bilal al-Khuza'i, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 624 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bilal, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished us with an admonition from which hearts trembled and eyes shed tears. We said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if it is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so enjoin upon us. He said: Hold to fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave; whoever of you lives after me will see much disagreement. So hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, guided caliphs - bite upon it with the molars; and beware of newly-invented matters, and every newly-invented matter is misguidance."
"16744","625 - Narrated to us Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi, narrated to us my father, (h). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us 'Ali ibn Bahr, (h). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri, narrated to us 'Abdah ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi, they said: Narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Musabbihat before sleeping, and said: In them is a verse better than a thousand verses."
"16745","626 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi', (h). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Mansur, (h). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar, narrated to us al-Hakam ibn Musa, they said: Narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, (h). And narrated to us Musa ibn 'Isa al-Himsi, narrated to us Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi, narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, both from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bilal al-Khuza'i, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The martyrs and those who died upon their beds will dispute before our Lord concerning those who died in the plague. The martyrs will say: Our brothers were killed as we were killed. The deceased upon their beds will say: Our brothers died upon their beds as we died. So Allah will judge between them, saying: Look at the wounds of the plague-stricken; if they resemble the wounds of the martyrs, then they are of them and with them. So they will look at the wounds of the plague-stricken, and they will resemble the wounds of the martyrs, so they will be joined with them."
"16746","Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-'Irbad. 627 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Himyar, narrated to us Fadalah ibn Sharik, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he stood one day among the people and said: O people, you are about to become armies: an army in Syria, an army in Iraq, and an army in Yemen. Ibn Hawalah said: O Messenger of Allah, if that time reaches me, choose for me. He said: I choose Syria for you, for it is the choice of the Muslims and Allah's chosen of His lands; He gathers to it His chosen of His creation. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its stagnant pools; for Allah has guaranteed for me Syria and its people."
"16747","Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 628 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis,i narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, (h). And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, they said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah, narrated to me Yunus ibn Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ruhm, that 'Irbad ibn Sariyah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited him to the predawn meal in Ramadan, saying: Come to the blessed morning meal."
"16748","And I heard him saying: O Allah, teach Mu'awiyah the Book and reckoning, and protect him from punishment."
"16749","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad. 629 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Sa'id ibn Suwayd, from 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am the servant of Allah and the seal of the prophets; Adam, peace be upon him, was yet lying in his clay. And I shall inform you of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of 'Isa, the vision of my mother which she saw - and likewise the mothers of the prophets see. The mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when she bore him, saw a light by which the palaces of Syria were illumined for her."
"16750","630 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi, narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Ayyash al-Himsi, narrated to us al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, narrated to me Suwayd ibn Sa'id, from 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am the servant of Allah and the seal of the prophets; Adam, peace be upon him, was yet lying in his clay. And I shall narrate to you of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of 'Isa, the vision of my mother which she saw - and likewise the mothers of the prophets see. The mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw, when she bore him, a light by which the palaces of Syria were illumined."
"16751","631 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hawtiyyan, they said: Narrated to us Abu al-Mughirah, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, (h). And narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, informed me Baqiyyah, informed me Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Suwayd al-Kalbi, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am with Allah in the Mother of the Book the seal of the prophets, while Adam was yet lying in his clay. And I shall narrate to you the interpretation of that: the supplication of Ibrahim, the supplication: {And send among them a messenger from themselves}; the glad tidings of 'Isa son of Maryam: {And giving glad tidings of a messenger to come after me, whose name is Ahmad}; and the vision of my mother - she saw in her sleep that she bore a light by which the palaces of Syria were illumined."
"16752","Suwayd ibn Jabalah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 632 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us my father, (h). And narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Harith, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, narrated to us Luqman ibn 'Amir, from Suwayd ibn Jabalah, from 'Irbad ibn Sariyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This ummah shall crowd upon the Pond as camels crowd that came for water after five days."
"16753","633 - And narrated to us 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us my father, (h). And narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq, narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Harith, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, narrated to us Luqman ibn 'Amir, from Suwayd ibn Jabalah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I take from a servant his two precious ones - while he is patient with them - I am not content with a reward for them less than Paradise, when he praises Allah for them."
"16754","634 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musaffa, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Uthman, from Luqman ibn 'Amir, from Suwayd ibn Jabalah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he raised it, he said: The Lord Mighty and Majestic said: When I take from My servant his two precious ones - while he clings to them - I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"16755","635 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Ishaq, narrated to us my father, (h). And narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq, they said: Narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from 'Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf, from Suwayd ibn Jabalah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the choicest of Paradise. A man of you says to his shepherd: Keep to the choicest of the valley, for it is the most fertile and most grassy."
"16756","Sa'id ibn Hani, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 636 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis,i narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, (h). And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, they said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Sa'id ibn Hani, that he heard 'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami saying: I sold to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a young camel. Then I came demanding payment, saying: Pay me for my young camel. He said: Yes, I shall surely pay you. So he paid me and paid me well. Then a bedouin came and said: Pay me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid him an aged camel, well advanced in age. He said: This is better than my young camel, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are the best of them in repayment."
"16757","Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-'Irbad. 637 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi and Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani, they said: Narrated to us Adam ibn Abi Iyas, narrated to us Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him that he heard 'Irbad ibn Sariyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would invoke blessings upon the foremost row three times, and upon the one after it once."
"16758","638 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, informed us 'Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Ma'mar and 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek forgiveness for the foremost row three times, and for the second once. Ma'mar and 'Ikrimah did not mention in their hadith Jubayr ibn Nufayr."
"16759","639 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, informed us Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek forgiveness for the foremost row three times, and for the second once. Hisham did not mention in the isnad Jubayr ibn Nufayr."
"16760","640 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati, narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Ammar, narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked blessings upon the foremost row three times, and upon the second once."
"16761","641 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi, narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Ayyash al-Himsi, (h). And narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Ammar, they said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, Kathir ibn Murrah and 'Amr ibn al-Aswad, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed is cut off from its owner when he dies, except one stationed guarding in the path of Allah; his deed grows for him and his provision flows upon him until the Day of Resurrection."
"16762","642 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us 'Isa ibn Yunus, from Abu Hamzah al-Himsi, from Sha'wadh al-Azdi, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) admonished us one day with an eloquent admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled. A man of the Muslims said: It is as if this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I have left you upon the clear white path, its night like its day; none of you deviates from it after me except one doomed. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement, so beware of innovations; hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided caliphs - bite upon it with the molars; and hold to hearing and obeying even if it be an Abyssinian slave."
"16763","Habib ibn 'Ubayd al-Rahabi, from al-'Irbad. 643 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, informed us Baqiyyah, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn 'Ubayd, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Mighty and Majestic says: When I take the two precious ones of My servant - while he clings to them - I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise, when he praises Me for them."
"16764","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 644 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Idris ibn 'Abd al-Karim al-Haddad al-Muqri, they said: Narrated to us al-Haytham ibn Kharijah, (h). And narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi, narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Safwan ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty says: Those who love one another for My majesty shall be in the shade of My Throne on a day when there is no shade but Mine."
"16765","Hakim ibn 'Umayr, from al-'Irbad. 645 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Himsi, narrated to us al-Musayyab ibn Wadih, narrated to us Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah, from Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir, from Hakim ibn 'Umayr, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Not lawful for you of beasts of prey is every fanged one, nor domestic donkeys; do not enter the houses of the People of the Book, nor consume their wealth except what they willingly permit; do not strike. Does a sated man of you think, reclining upon his couch, saying: Allah Mighty and Majestic forbade nothing except in the Qur'an? Nay, by Allah, I have narrated and commanded and admonished."
"16766","Khalid ibn Yazid, from al-'Irbad. 646 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, from 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man gives his wife water to drink, he is rewarded. He said: So I stood to her and gave her water to drink, and informed her of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16767","Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah. 647 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuma-ni, narrated to us 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, from Abu Hazim, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays an obligatory prayer has an answered supplication; and whoever completes the Qur'an has an answered supplication."
"16768","Umm Habibah bint al-'Irbad, from her father. 648 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, from Wahb ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Narrated to us Umm Habibah bint al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every fanged beast of prey, every taloned bird, forbade animals tied up for target practice, and that pregnant captives be approached until they deliver what is in their wombs."
"16769","649 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, narrated to us Wahb ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to me Umm Habibah bint al-'Irbad, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a tuft of wool from the fay' and said: I have of this only what one of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you; so return the needle and the thread, and beware of misappropriation, for it is disgrace and shame."
"16770","650 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb, narrated to us Abu 'Asim, from Wahb ibn Abi Khalid, from Umm Habibah bint al-'Irbad, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar domestic donkeys."
"16771","651 - And with its isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar stealthy pillaging."
"16772","Unnamed men, from al-'Irbad. 652 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to me Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn 'Ubayd, from one who narrated to him, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the slaughtered animals of the Christians and their festivals. He said: If you do not eat it, then feed me."
"16773","653 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musaffa, narrated to us Baqiyyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from a man of Quraysh, from a man he named, from al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever licks the plate and licks his fingers, Allah will satiate him in this world and the Hereafter."
"16774","Chapter of Ghayn: those named Gharafah. Gharafah ibn al-Harith al-Azdi al-Kindi. 654 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me Harmalah ibn 'Imran, narrated to me Ka'b ibn 'Alqamah, that Gharafah ibn al-Harith - and he had Companionship, and fought with 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl in Yemen in the Ridda - that a Christian of the people of Egypt called al-Mandaqun passed by, and he invited him to Islam. The Christian mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and reviled him. That was reported to 'Amr ibn al-'As, who sent for him and said: We have given him a covenant. Gharafah said: Allah forbid that we gave them covenants and pledges that they harm us concerning Allah and His Messenger; we gave them only that we leave them with their churches, saying therein what they wish, that we not burden them beyond their capacity, that we fight in their defense, and that they be left with their laws unless they come to us and we judge between them by what Allah revealed. 'Amr ibn al-'As said: You have spoken truly."
"16775","655 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Habban al-Nasri, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Harmalah ibn 'Imran, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Azdi, from Gharafah ibn al-Harith, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage; the camels for sacrifice were brought, and he said: Call for me Abu Hasan. So 'Ali was called. He said: Take the lower part of the spear. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took its upper part, and we cut the camels with it. When he finished, he mounted the mule and took 'Ali behind him."
"16776","Ghaziyyah ibn al-Harith al-Ansari. 656 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam, informed me Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Rafi', from Ghaziyyah ibn al-Harith, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no emigration after the conquest; it is only three: jihad, intention, and gathering."
"16777","657 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to us al-Layth, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, (h). And narrated to us Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-'Attar and Muhammad ibn 'Ali, the two Makkans, they said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Mansur, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me 'Amr ibn al-Harith, that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Rafi', from Ghaziyyah ibn al-Harith, that he informed him, that youths of Quraysh wanted to emigrate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but their fathers prevented them. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the conquest; it is only jihad and intention."
"16778","Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi. 658 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Dashtaki al-Razi, narrated to us al-Harith ibn Muslim, from Bahr al-Saqqa', from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Umar: that a man of Thaqif called Ghaylan ibn Salamah became Muslim while having ten wives. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to choose four of them and leave six."
"16779","659 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi and Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Ibn Yazid, from 'Urwah, from Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi: that Nafi' was a slave of Ghaylan ibn Salamah, and fled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became Muslim while Ghaylan was a polytheist; then Ghaylan became Muslim, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him his allegiance."
"16780","660 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to me Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah, narrated to us Mu'alla ibn Mansur, narrated to us Shabib ibn Shaybah, from Bishr ibn 'Asim al-Thaqafi, from Ghaylan ibn Salamah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his journey, and he said: If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband."
"16781","Ghudayf ibn al-Harith al-Kindi. 661 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il, narrated to us 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah, from Makhul, from 'A'idh Allah Abu Idris, from Ghudayf or Abu Ghusayf, a Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever introduces satire into Islam, cut off his tongue."
"16782","Ghutayf Abu 'Iyad. 662 - Narrated to us Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Hawti, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi', narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Sa'id ibn Salim al-Kindi, from Mu'awiyah ibn 'Iyad ibn Ghutayf, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man drinks wine, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, kill him."
"16783","Ghalib ibn Abjar al-Muzani. 663 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated to us 'Abd al-Mu'min ibn 'Abd Allah Abu al-Hasan, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-'Absi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani, from Ghalib ibn Abjar, he said: Qays was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Qays, may Allah have mercy on Qays. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, do you invoke mercy upon Qays? He said: Yes, he was upon the religion of my father Isma'il son of Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah. O Qays, greet Yemen; O Yemen, greet Qays. Qays are Allah's horsemen on earth. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, there shall come upon people a time when none supports this religion but Qays. Allah Mighty and Majestic has horsemen of the people of heaven, marked, and horsemen of the people of earth, distinguished; the horsemen of Allah of the people of earth are Qays. Qays is but an egg split from us, the People of the House. Qays is Allah's lions on earth - meaning lions of Allah."
"16784","664 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi, narrated to us 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath, narrated to me my father, from Abu 'Umays, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, from Ghalib ibn Abjar, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my family's food but donkeys I have. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed your family of the fat of your wealth, for I have deemed filthy the roaming scavengers of the town."
"16785","665 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us my father, (h). And narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: Narrated to us Waki', from Mis'ar, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Ibn Ma'qil al-Muzani, from people of Muzaynah the pure, from Ghalib ibn al-Abjar, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Nothing remains of my wealth but donkeys. He said: Feed your family of the fat of your wealth, for I have disliked for you the roaming scavengers of the town."
"16786","666 - Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Mis'ar, from 'Ubayd ibn Hasan, from 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, from two men of Muzaynah, one from the other, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir ibn Luwaym and Ghalib ibn Abjar - Mis'ar said: I think Ghalib is the one who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth with which to feed my family but donkeys. He said: Then feed your family of the fat of your wealth, for I forbid for you the scavengers of the town."
"16787","667 - Narrated to us Mahmud ibn 'Ali al-Bazzar al-Asbahani, narrated to us Yunus ibn Habib, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Shu'bah, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, he said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil narrating from 'Abd Allah ibn Busr, from people of Muzaynah, that Abjar or Ibn Abjar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth but donkeys. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed your family of the fat of your wealth; I have only disliked for you the scavengers of the town."
"16788","668 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi 'Umar al-'Adani, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Mis'ar, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from a man, from two men of Muzaynah who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A year of drought struck us - and he mentioned the hadith."
"16789","669 - Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh, narrated to us Sharik, from Mansur, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Ghalib ibn Duraykh, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, famine struck us, and the fat of our wealth is donkeys. He said: Eat of the fat of your wealth - and he said - I have only deemed filthy for you, or disliked for you, the dung-eating scavengers of the town."
"16790","670 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Sharik, from Mansur, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Ghalib ibn Duraykh, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a year of drought struck us, and the fat of our wealth is in donkeys. He said: Eat of the fat of your wealth, for I have only deemed filthy the scavengers of the town."
"16791","Chapter of Fa': those named Fadl. Fadl ibn al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, and his mother: Umm al-Fadl, whose name is Lubabah bint al-Harith ibn Hazn ibn Bujayr ibn al-Haram ibn Ruwaybah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Hilal ibn 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah, or Umm al-Fadl bint 'Amr ibn Ka'b. 671 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Madini Fustuqah, narrated to us Dawud ibn Rushayd, from al-Haytham ibn 'Adi, he said: Al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas died four years before his father, in the year twenty-eight. They differed concerning the death of al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas: some people said: He was martyred in Syria on the day of Ajnadayn; and it is said: On the day of Marj al-Suffar - both days being in the year eighteen; and he died at twenty-one years of age."
"16792","'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, from his brother al-Fadl: 'Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas. 672 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Musa ibn Harun, they said: Narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (h). And narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Abu al-Sha'tha', they said: Narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-'Aqabah, stoning it with seven pebbles, magnifying Allah with each pebble."
"16793","673 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Awn ibn Sallam, narrated to us Yahya ibn al-'Ala', from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him behind him on the morning of Muzdalifah, and continued uttering the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-'Aqabah. He said: He stoned it from beneath it with seven pebbles, magnifying with each pebble once. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed and said: I have sacrificed here, and Mina is all a place of sacrifice; so sacrifice in your dwellings."
"16794","674 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Salt, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather 'Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed at the Jamrat al-'Aqabah and said: I have sacrificed here, and Mina is all a place of sacrifice; so sacrifice in your dwellings."
"16795","Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl. 675 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Kufi, (h). And narrated to us 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, narrated to us Yusuf ibn 'Adi, (h). And narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Musa ibn Harun, they said: Narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: Narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said: Al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas said: I was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I kept hearing him uttering the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-'Aqabah; when he stoned it, he stopped the talbiyah. And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi'."
"16796","676 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il, narrated to us Zuhayr, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, 'Ikrimah and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uttered the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-'Aqabah."
"16797","677 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari, narrated to us Safwan ibn 'Isa al-Zuhri, informed us al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas - al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, my brother, informed me, he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me behind him on the morning of Muzdalifah. He said: A bedouin man set out with us, with him a beautiful daughter of his, walking alongside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he turned my face away from her. He kept uttering the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"16798","678 - Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih and Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas - and he was the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Muzdalifah - he said: I kept hearing him uttering the tahlil until he reached the Jamrah; when he stoned with it, he stopped."
"16799","679 - Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn 'Imran al-Sadusi, narrated to us Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf, narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid and 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: I do not like to pray in the Ka'bah; whoever prays in it has left something behind him. But my brother narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered it, fell between the two pillars prostrating, then sat sitting, and did not pray."
"16800","'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl. 680 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas - al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, and he was the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day - that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uttering the tahlil until he stoned the Jamrat al-'Aqabah."
